\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Follows Baht, Rupiah To End Lower \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2000\par 11:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar followed the rupiah and baht to end higher on Tuesday as participants liquidated long U.S. dollar positions to lock in profits. \par \par \uc2  Around 0935 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7453, down from S$1.7475 late Monday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar approached the key resistance level of S$1.7500 in early trading, moving as high as S$1.7485 before dropping off quickly. \par \par \uc2  The level of S$1.7500 is widely seen as one at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  One trader said the U.S. dollar could drop as low as S$1.7350 in coming days, adding that stop-loss orders have been placed at levels of between 1.7390 and 1.7420 by participants with long U.S.-dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  A stronger Singapore dollar bolstered the government bond market somewhat, pushing yields down slightly. The yield on the seven-year bond fell to 4.21% from 4.22% late Monday, while the yield on the 10-year bond fell to 4.56% from 4.57%. \par \par \uc2  Money market rates were slightly lower on profit-taking after creeping up for several days on concerns about the possible inflationary impact of higher oil prices. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore announced it would lower, the tier one capital ratio for banks to 8% from 10%, on Sept. 30. The overall capital adequacy ratio remains unchanged at 12%. \par \par \uc2  In the longer term, the move is expected to boost lending by banks by reducing the amount of shareholders' equity they must keep as a proportion of their assets. The remainder of the capital requirement can be fulfilled with subordinated debt. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But because demand for bank loans remains sluggish and most banks have\par capital ratios of 15% or more, it will be several months before the move\par has any discernible impact on bank lending, analysts said.\par               Late Tuesday         Late Monday\par            bid      offer           bid     offer\par Overnight  2.0000%  2.1250%        1.7500%  1.8750%\par 3 Month    2.4375%  2.5625%        2.5000%  2.6250%\par 1 Year     2.6875%  2.8125%        2.7500%  2.8750%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Christopher Wellisz, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4802;\par christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9j04hhq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
