\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Down Late; Won Bears Brunt Of Sell Off \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 995 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2000\par 10:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The South Korean won continued to lead the downward spiral in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Monday, as the bloodbath on the Seoul bourse and doubts on the country's debt restructuring efforts triggered a wave of panic selling in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Reflecting the international strength of the U.S. dollar, better-than-expected economic data out of Thailand and Singapore even failed to provide much reprieve for those local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "It's not just the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are weak, but all the other emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. "The dollar is strong globally and oil prices are high, affecting many emerging markets." \par \par \uc2  Like the rest of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Thai baht and the Singapore dollar caved in to the gloom pervading the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  collapsed below the psychologically-important support level of 42 baht against the dollar to hit a 25-month low. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  threatened to test the key S$1.7500 psychological resistance mark, but retreated on fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won felt the brunt of the selling frenzy in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, as the local stock market posted its second-biggest daily drop this year, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 1,131.40 won, up from Friday's close of KRW1,119.90 and its highest close since June 1, when it ended at KRW1,132. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Korea Composite Stock Price Index plunged 8.1% to end at 577.56, its lowest finish since March 10, 1999, when it ended at 569.27. \par \par \uc2  Ford Motor Co's announcement last Friday that it won't make a final bid for struggling Daewoo Motor continued to worry investors, as it cast doubts on South Korea's efforts to restructure its debt-ridden industries, market observers said. \par \par \uc2  Market sentiment was also bruised by escalating crude oil prices and falling dynamic random access memory chip prices, which have reinforced the bleak outlook for the semiconductor industry, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had jumped to as high as KRW1,138 in intraday trading, but profit-taking in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar-selling by exporters, especially after the stock market closed, helped the won recoup the bulk of its losses, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The won rebounded quite impressively, but the market is still shaky," said Suktae Oh, a Seoul-based economist at Salomon Smith Barney/Citibank. "The market will restore some of its stability, but at higher levels than maybe about two weeks ago." \par \par \uc2  The dollar will likely consolidate between KRW1,120 and KRW1,130 in the short term as panic-selling in the won dies down, said Suktae Oh. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With the won's steep decline largely sentiment-driven, "everybody\par would agree that this would not be a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crisis," Oh said.\par - - 18/09/00 08-36G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The New Taiwan dollar too succumbed to lofty oil prices, a slumping\par local stock market and falling dynamic random access memory chip prices\par earlier in the session, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But armed with its vast cache of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, Taiwan's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped up its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to a degree not seen since the\par regional financial crisis to stem the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's losses, dealers\par said. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  accounted for around US$400 million of the day's\par US$689 million turnover, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar closed at NT$31.255, compared with the previous close\par of NT$31.268. Before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in, the U.S. dollar had\par risen as high as NT$31.340.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Southeast Asia, the Thai baht looks poised to test its next\par downside target of THB42.50 to the dollar soon, and thereafter THB43 in\par coming months, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar rose to THB42.195 around 0925 GMT, compared with THB41.925\par late Friday, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar's strength against regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , local demand to\par repay foreign debt and mounting political anxieties ahead of elections,\par expected between late November and January, helped extend the baht's\par recent descent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand's better-than-expected economic report card failed to\par alleviate the pressure on the baht, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand's gross domestic product rose 6.6% on-year in the second\par quarter of 2000, well above a consensus forecast of 5.5%. Second-quarter\par economic growth was higher than a revised 5.3% year-on-year expansion in\par the first quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Similarly, stronger-than-expected trade data did little to boost the\par Singapore dollar, which instead found respite on talk that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore might defend the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around S$1.7500\par against the U.S. dollar, dealers said. The MAS is believed to have\par defended the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around S$1.7515 against the U.S. dollar on\par July 24.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore's non-oil domestic exports grew 27.3% to S$10.71 billion in\par August from a year earlier, exceeding analysts' consensus forecast of\par 15.3% growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the Philippines, ailing regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , combined with\par uncertainties over the outcome of fighting between government forces and\par Muslim rebels on Jolo island, as the military continued its massive\par assault to rescue 19 hostages, dented the peso, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso's decline was, however, tempered by fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , they added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar closed at 45.820 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up\par from PHP45.590 Friday, but down from Monday's intraday high of\par PHP45.880.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the dollar was at 8,655 rupiah,\par down slightly from IDR8,685 late Friday, on dollar-selling by offshore\par participants and Indonesian state banks, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807;\par netty.ismail@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9i04ios\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
