\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah rebounds, possible c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2000\par 11:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah rebounded in late trade on Thursday on speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We assume the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling dollars through the state banks," a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  By 0930 GMT the local unit had clawed back to 8,565/8,595 against the dollar from 8,835/8,855 in early trade when it was still reeling from a massive car bomb explosion at the Jakarta stock exchange building that killed 15 people the day before. \par \par \uc2  Apart from some limited profit taking, dealers - who earlier tipped the market would test 9,000 against the dollar - otherwise struggled to explain the market's about turn. \par \par \uc2  "It must be due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...the only other reason is that \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been very long dollars for the past three days and when the market started to turn they started selling," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Now it will be fairly hard to touch 9,000," he added. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off news late on Thursday of more bomb threats made against key buildings in the capital. \par \par \uc2  State-owned Bank Mandiri told Reuters it received two threats after lunch. The Surabaya stock exchange office in Jakarta received four threats. \par \par \uc2  The market also paid no attention to the resumption of the graft trial of former President Suharto on Thursday. The former autocrat did not appear due to ill health. \par \par \uc2  Despite the rupiah's recovery, Wednesday's explosion, which was the latest in a series to hit key targets in the capital, is likely to further dent investor confidence. \par \par \uc2  Market sentiment has also been dampened by the murder of three U.N. aid workers in the West Timor border town of Atambua last week which has angered the international community. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9e08595\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
