\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late On Long USD Liquidation; Bonds Flat \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2000\par 11:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was higher late Thursday on liquidation of long U.S. dollar positions by banks amid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Government bonds ended nearly flat after market participants bought back the securities they had sold earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  Around 0848 GMT (4:48 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7391, down from S$1.7440 late Wednesday in Asia, and down form an intraday high of S$1.7460 reached in early trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that the U.S. dollar's failure to break above 8,900 rupiah and fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at levels over S$1.7450 prompted banks to liquidate long U.S. dollar positions against both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke below initial support at S$1.7400, but is expected to find stronger support at S$1.7380, dealers said. Resistance remains at S$1.7450. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, government bonds were sold early on weaker regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but were bought back in the afternoon following strong recoveries by the rupiah and the Singapore dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trading, bond prices were nearly unchanged and their yields flat. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank money market, the overnight rate eased on flush liquidity, while volatility on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the one-year rate slightly higher. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par            Late Thursday            Late Wednesday\par            bid      offer           bid     offer\par Overnight  1.3750%  1.5000%         1.7500%  1.8750%\par 3 Month    2.5000%  2.6250%         2.4375%  2.5625%\par 1 Year     2.7500%  2.8750%         2.6875%  2.8125%\par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4809;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par -0- 14/09/00 09-06G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9e04hef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
