\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late After Rupiah Recoups Loss \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 900 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2000\par 10:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed late Thursday, after the Indonesian unit's failure to test the psychologically-important 9,000 rupiah support level helped most of its other Southeast Asian counterparts recoup their losses, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah, the Singapore dollar and the Philippine peso were firmer, while the Thai baht continued to be weighed on by dollar demand from corporates and offshore players, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In Northeast Asia, a slide in the local stock markets and a weaker yen dented the South Korean won and the New Taiwan dollar, although aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  staunched the latter \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar-selling by state banks and profit-taking by offshore participants salvaged the rupiah, which had earlier in the day threatened to test the psychologically-important IDR9,000 level. \par \par \uc2  Around 0820 GMT, the dollar was at IDR8,575, down from IDR8,775 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had advanced to as high as IDR8,890 in early trading Thursday, extending late Wednesday's sharp losses. A powerful explosion that ripped through the basement carpark of the Jakarta Stock Exchange Building late Wednesday dealt a fresh blow to sentiment, already bruised by mounting concerns over political and social instability in the country. \par \par \uc2  "The bombing itself is negative in terms of the investment attractiveness of the country," said Philip Wee, a treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  The explosion took place just a day before the resumption of former president Suharto's corruption trial. As widely expected by the market, the trial was adjourned for a second time Thursday when the court appointed an independent medical team to determine whether he is fit to stand trial. \par \par \uc2  However, the rupiah's swift pullback Thursday doesn't herald a recovery for the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which will likely remain vulenerable to the country's political and social malaise, some analysts said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wee at Standard Chartered Bank said the rupiah is technically poised\par to hit IDR9,200 to the dollar "in the next couple of weeks."\par - - 14/09/00 08-54G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar also recovered sharply, with the U.S. dollar\par falling back below S$1.7400 psychological support, thanks to a reversal\par in the rupiah's fortunes and the euro's rebound.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the\par U.S. dollar's recent run-up peaked at S$1.7459 early Thursday, also\par fueled profit-taking in the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0945 GMT (5:45 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7392, down\par from S$1.7445 late Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro was at $0.8697, compared with $0.8591 late Wednesday in New\par York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Manila, the dollar ended at 45.605 pesos on the Philippine Dealing\par System, after climbing to as high as PHP45.95 early Thursday, its\par strongest level against the Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since touching PHP46.50\par Jan. 7, 1998. The dollar closed at PHP45.690 Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine budget deficit in the first eight months of the year\par reached PHP69.78 billion, already exceeding the government's PHP62.5\par billion full-year target, the government said late Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although this was unsurprising, market participants might use this as\par an excuse to push the peso lower Friday, some dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In contrast, the Thai baht benefited little from the rebound of its\par Southeast Asian counterparts. Political concerns ahead of the country's\par general elections, expected to take place in the fourth quarter, and\par strong corporate demand for dollars ahead of the half-year book closing\par continued to weigh on the baht, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar briefly touched a two-year high of 41.85 baht in early\par trading, but rapidly pulled back on reported comments by Thai Deputy\par Premier Supachai Panitchpakdi that he was "concerned" about the baht's\par weakness, and that he would discuss it at the weekly economic ministers'\par meeting Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Late Thursday, the dollar was at THB41.725, up from THB41.655 late\par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul's remarks Thursday\par that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saw no need to defend the baht at the moment gave\par participants the greenlight to push down the baht again.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, foreign equity fund outflows, which contributed to a slide\par on the South Korean bourse, the bearish sentiment toward the\par semiconductor industry and a weaker yen hammered the South Korean won,\par dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar closed at 1,115.1 won, up from last Friday's close of\par KRW1,108.5. Korean financial markets were closed Monday through\par Wednesday for the Korean Thanksgiving holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the Japanese yen, the dollar was quoted at Y107.21, up from\par Y107.12 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y106.95 late\par Wednesday in Tokyo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The New Taiwan dollar closed at a new eight-month low against its U.S.\par counterpart on continued U.S. dollar-buying in the non-deliverable\par forward market and a slump on the local bourse, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar ended at NT$31.125, up from NT$31.112 late Wednesday.\par Thursday's close was the lowest level since Dec. 30, 1999, when the New\par Taiwan dollar finished at NT$31.395.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807;\par netty.ismail@dowjones.com\par -0- 14/09/00 10-38G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9e04hc7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
