\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Tracks Regionals Lower Late; Bond Ylds Flat \b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2000\par 12:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Weaker regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the euro dragged the Singapore dollar lower against its U.S. counterpart late Thursday, while bond yields ended flat, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0939 GMT (5:39 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7306, up from S$1.7290 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  U.S. dollar buying by banks and offshore market participants lifted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday high of S$1.7325. \par \par \uc2  However, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surrendered some gains in the afternoon on profit-taking and fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. names sold (U.S. dollars), and a local bank also did so but we don't think it was on behalf of the MAS," a chief dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  "On the whole the U.S. dollar is looking somewhat bearish (compared with) yesterday," he added. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. bank dealer added that market participants were still interested in buying U.S. dollars and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could make further gains against its Singapore and Thai counterparts if oil prices remain high. \par \par \uc2  The price of U.S. benchmark crude oil futures has risen to a new post-Gulf War high above US$35 a barrel. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the U.S. dollar to be supported around S$1.7290 overnight, and capped at S$1.7335 by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the last apparent MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  six weeks ago happened around the S$1.7330 to S$1.7340 level. \par \par \uc2  In the bond market, Singapore government bond prices fell slightly on light selling, but the price change was too small to affect yields. \par \par \uc2  Bonds are usually sold when the Singapore dollar weakens, but market participants have already priced in the weaker local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and aren't selling heavily, a local dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Also, with flush liquidity keeping short-term money market rates steady at low levels there is little incentive to sell, he adds. \par \par \uc2  Bond yields were flat, with the yield on the benchmark 10-year bond closing at 4.56%, and the five-and seven-year yields at 4.21% and 3.84%, respectively. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank money market, interest rates were mostly steady on flush market liquidity. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par            Late Tuesday             Late Wednesday\par            bid      offer           bid     offer\par Overnight  2.0000%  2.2500%         2.2500%  2.3750%\par 3 Month    2.4375%  2.5625%         2.4375%  2.5625%\par 1 Year     2.6250%  2.7500%         2.6250%  2.7500%\par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4809;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par -0- 07/09/00 10-03G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9704cyl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
