\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Trapped in ranges, eyeing rupiah. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,038 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2000\par 03:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Aug 30 (Reuters) - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  stuck in ranges in early Wednesday trade, feeling the \par \par \uc2  conflicting effects of the still strong yen and \par \par \uc2  lingering political concerns in Indonesia and the Philippines. \par \par \uc2      Most units were barely changed compared to levels seen late \par \par \uc2  the previous day, with only the rupiah looking vulnerable \par \par \uc2  around 8,380 per dollar. \par \par \uc2      Political and economic concerns also kept the peso within \par \par \uc2  arm's reach of recent 30-month lows. \par \par \uc2      The yen held firm around 106 per dollar on confidence \par \par \uc2  Japanese markets would benefit from continued growth in Japan. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said an a lower than expected 0.7 percent fall in \par \par \uc2  July industrial production month-on-month did not detract from \par \par \uc2  recovery hopes. \par \par \uc2      The spotlight trailed on the euro, sterling and Swiss \par \par \uc2  franc \par \par \uc2  after they slid against the dollar and yen overnight amid \par \par \uc2  speculation the European economy had passed its peak. \par \par \uc2  Sterling extended its losses in Tokyo trade, hitting a \par \par \uc2  seven year low against the dollar on expectations rates would \par \par \uc2  be kept on hold. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah recouped part of its early losses but remained \par \par \uc2  shaky amid caution towards the country's new economic team and \par \par \uc2  parliamentary probe into Wahid-linked scandals. \par \par \uc2  New chief economics minister Rizal Ramli said he had \par \par \uc2  indicated to IMF First Deputy Managing Director Stanley Fischer \par \par \uc2  some conditions in the current of intent might not be \par \par \uc2  applicable. \par \par \uc2  Ramli said the new government wanted to first study the \par \par \uc2  letter, signed on July 31, and that this was the reason Jakarta \par \par \uc2  had asked the IMF to postpone a board meeting this week. \par \par \uc2      The basis of the meeting was to be discussions for a new \par \par \uc2  cash injection for Indonesia. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said trade was thin and the mood volatile though \par \par \uc2  strong rupiah support was seen around 8,420 points. \par \par \uc2      Singapore's United Overseas Bank said in a research note it \par \par \uc2  advocated buying on dollar dips to 8,100/200. Its end-2000 \par \par \uc2  target was 8,500 to 8,800 per dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso clung to levels of around 45 per dollar despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par news the economy had grown a faster-than-expected 4.5 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year-on-year in the second quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the government's widening budget deficit and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par concern over a Moslem insurgency in the south continued to dog\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the spotlight was the latest kidnapping of an American\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by Abu Sayyaf guerrillas who still hold six Europeans and a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Filipino hostage.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Six Western hostages have been released by the rebels over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the last two days.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Separately, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the better-than-expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GDP data did not warrant cutting its widely watched overnight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par borrowing rate which currently stands at 10 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht dipped alongside the rupiah in early trade, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par onshore parties bidding actively for dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the market seemed to have finally reacted to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par news of the government allowing the state-owned power firm EGAT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to raise 5.3 billion baht from the local bond market to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par refinance its foreign debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The move would further add pressure to the baht as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par company is expected to enter the market in the near future to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buy yen and dollars to repay its debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "They are unlikely to buy all in one go, and I doubt if\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they have to cover the whole amount in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. But\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still, this is a big amount and it will definitely weigh on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht," said a dealer at a European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the macro front, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will publish key\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monthly economic data on Thursday and the Commerce Ministry\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par will release price data on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar lost some ground in early trade as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign names bid for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par faltered.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The unit move in a narrow 1.7204-1.7220 band, with dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par anticipating range-trade ahead.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     While the rupiah only makes up a small proportion of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local unit's nominal effective exchange rate in terms of its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade weighted index, sentiment can be affected due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore's strong trade and investment ties with Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Most analysts remain bullish on Singapore's economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outlook, and expect a gradual appreciation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SEB Merchant Banking forecast in its latest report that the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing dollar would move to 1.69 by end-2000 and 1.63 by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mid-2001.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab    -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won flirted with a fresh 16-week closing high at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par open as dollars from exporters and foreigners keen to buy local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks filtered through.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Seoul dealers said exporters were unloading dollars to meet\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par end-month won fund demands and that foreign investors were seen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying into KOSPI stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors have been net buyers of 1.5 trillion won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par worth of Korea stocks so far this month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Despite a recent protest by some local and foreign dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against frequent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the authorities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were seen defending the 1,108 per dollar level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar was underpinned by foreign fund inflows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and demand from local parties covering their month-end\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Players were reluctant to push the Taiwan dollar much lower\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par given the recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to shore up the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unit, dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On Tuesday, foreign funds bought a net T$719 million in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan stocks on Tuesday against net selling of T$172 million\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     106.25\tab  106.62\tab    +0.35\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7214\tab  1.7204\tab    -0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    31.070\tab  31.070\tab    +0.00\par  Korean won   1109.10\tab 1110.00\tab    +0.08\par  Baht\tab      40.94\tab   40.89\tab    -0.12\par  Peso\tab      45.06\tab   45.01\tab    -0.10\par  Rupiah\tab  8390.00\tab 8325.00\tab    -0.77\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     106.25\tab  102.21\tab    -3.80\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7214\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.33\par  Taiwan dlr    31.070\tab  31.380\tab    +1.00\par  Korean won   1109.10\tab 1135.00\tab    +2.34\par  Baht\tab      40.94\tab   37.45\tab    -8.52\par  Peso\tab      45.06\tab   40.20\tab   -10.78\par  Rupiah\tab  83