\par\par \b \uc2  Sing dlr extends gains despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk. \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2000\par 08:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Aug 10 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar extended gains in afternoon trade on Thursday, briefly piercing the key 1.7100 level despite talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market to rein in its sharp appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said injured dollar bulls stumbled into the market to cover short Sing dollar positions after it was strongly boosted by robust growth data and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comment it saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciating over the next 12 months. \par \par \uc2  "There were bouts of profit taking on the Sing dollar which helped slow down its pace...but only a bit. At one point, it breached 1.7100," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  "There are lots of stop-loss orders above that level. So, I reckon it would move much higher once the 1.7100 level is convincingly broken," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0623 GMT, the Sing dollar was quoted around 1.7115/1.7125, its best levels since a May 2 high of 1.7085, according to Reuters Graphics data. \par \par \uc2  Singapore posted robust year-on-year GDP growth of 8.0 percent for the second quarter, bringing growth for the first half to 8.8 percent. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said they did not see much further upside for the Sing dollar because the authorities were likely to step in to smooth sharp moves. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was also looking oversold against the Sing with a reading of 19.5 on the 14-day relative strength index, below the 30 oversold mark. \par \par \uc2  "The Sing dollar had been unjustifiably weak for a while because investors used it as a funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Now a lot of them are being caught short," said Fong Cheng Hong, head of treasury research at DBS Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "But going forward, I think the pace of appreciation should slow down a bit. The rise is a bit overdone, and I wouldn't be surprised if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes in to smooth it out." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore has said in the past that it does not comment on its market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but does \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb volatility. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8a0b7wy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
