\par\par \b \uc2  POLL-Singapore dlr seen rising to 1.70 by end-2000. \b0\par\par\uc2 613 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2000\par 08:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, Aug 3 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar\tab   is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to rise to 1.70 against the U.S. dollar by end-2000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  and to 1.67 by the middle of next year, a Reuters poll showed \par \par \uc2  on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      But forecasts were wide ranging with the 10 economists \par \par \uc2  polled on the Sing dollar's outlook for this year seeing it \par \par \uc2  between 1.66 and 1.74. Six economists polled on its outlook in \par \par \uc2  mid-2001 expected it to be in a 1.63 to 1.70 range. \par \par \uc2      The Sing dollar, which had plummeted to 22-month lows \par \par \uc2  before comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) \par \par \uc2  last week that it would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gradually \par \par \uc2  appreciate, has been steadily climbing. \par \par \uc2      It was off its highs by midday on Thursday after breaching \par \par \uc2  the 1.7280 technical barrier overnight. \par \par \uc2      At 0555 GMT, it was quoted at 1.7258/65. \par \par \uc2      In announcing its willingness to allow a stronger Sing \par \par \uc2  dollar, the MAS said consumer price inflation was expected to \par \par \uc2  edge up slightly to one to two percent over the next two years \par \par \uc2  as the labour market tightened and higher commodity prices \par \par \uc2  filtered through. \par \par \uc2  Cindy Chua, economist at Kay Hian, expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments to be realised by a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation to 1.71 \par \par \uc2  by year-end, adding the US dollar in general would also lose \par \par \uc2  some of its recent strength. \par \par \uc2  But JP Morgan economist Tan Tzu Ping, who forecast an \par \par \uc2  end-2000 level of 1.73, said the MAS was only sending a signal \par \par \uc2  and actual upward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be coming \par \par \uc2  soon. \par \par \uc2      "You're likely not to see an immediate change. The comments \par \par \uc2  were a warning shot across the bow," he said. \par \par \uc2      The MAS intention to use the Singapore dollar to stamp out \par \par \uc2  inflationary sparks comes amid a still fragile Southeast Asian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  environment. \par \par \uc2      That climate was linked to a generally lower level seen for \par \par \uc2  the Singapore dollar at the end of the year and at mid-2001. \par \par \uc2      A similar poll taken on May 19 had produced average levels \par \par \uc2  of 1.66 and 1.64, respectively. \par \par \uc2      "Our 1.73 (forecast) does assess the region as more \par \par \uc2  volatile, and while these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not heavily weighted \par \par \uc2  for the Sing... On the risk and policy side, there have been \par \par \uc2  negative repercussions," said Morgan's Tan. \par \par \uc2      Until the MAS comments, the market had believed \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  authorities were relaxed about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  decline, and previous \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been seen as simply a smoothing exercise. \par \par \uc2      The strength of the U.S. unit against the yen and euro, all \par \par \uc2  believed to be in the undisclosed basket of trade-weighted \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  the MAS uses to manage the exchange rate, was also \par \par \uc2  seen as key to the Singapore dollar's performance, analysts \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      The underlying good performance of the economy will also \par \par \uc2  tend to lend support to the local dollar. \par \par \uc2      "We are seeing some gradual firming of the Sing dollar \par \par \uc2  because the underlying economic fundamentals are still very \par \par \uc2  good," said Kaan Quan Hon, economist at DBS Securities. \par \par \uc2      Projections for the Singapore dollar versus the U.S. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar:     INSTITUTIONS:\tab \tab     DEC 00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par JUNE 01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ABN AMRO\tab \tab \tab      1.66\tab \tab    n/a*\par     DBS Securities\tab \tab      1.70\tab \tab    n/a*\par     GK Goh\tab \tab \tab \tab  1.70\tab \tab    1.67\par     JM Sassoon\tab \tab \tab    1.74\tab \tab    n/a*\par     JP Morgan\tab \tab \tab     1.73\tab \tab    1.70\par     Kay Hian\tab \tab \tab      1.71\tab \tab    n/a*\par     MMS/Standard & Poor's\tab     1.70\tab \tab    1.69\par     IDEAglobal.com\tab \tab      1.69\tab \tab    1.65\par     Standard Chartered\tab \tab  1.69\tab \tab    1.63\par     Vickers Ballas\tab \tab      1.71\tab \tab    1.70\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Average\tab \tab \tab \tab 1.70\tab \tab    1.67\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * No forecasts for mid-2001\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Singapore newsroom (65) 870 3080 fax:(65) 776 8112\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab singapore.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw83010ak\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
