\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Higher Late; Tracks Regionals; Bks Sell USD \b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2000\par 11:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is higher late Tuesday in line with stronger regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly the Thai baht, dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0834 GMT (14:34 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7320, down from S$1.7330 late Monday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said market sentiment toward the U.S. dollar is weak and its decline against other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  encouraged market participants to continue selling it for Singapore dollars. \par \par \uc2  Early U.S. dollar selling by a U.K. bank and an investment house in Hong Kong briefly took the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below S$1.7300 before buying by local companies pulled it back above that level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers, however, expect the U.S. dollar to stay above S$1.7300 in European and U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  On the upside, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to be capped by offers around S$1.7330. \par \par \uc2  "It is rumored that MAS agents are interested in offering (U.S. dollars) around S$1.7350-60, so the upside is limited," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Early last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to a 22-month high of S$1.7515. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar rose sharply last week after the MAS said Thursday it was prepared to allow a gradual and modest appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4809; amit.prakash@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw8103qye\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
