\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Chilled by Nasdaq, Nikkei breaches 16,000. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Yonggi Kang \par \uc2 1,108 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2000\par 12:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 28 (Reuters) - Hefty losses on the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Nasdaq overnight took a toll across most Asian stock markets on \par \par \uc2  Friday. \par \par \uc2      The exception was Taiwan, boosted by state fund buying. \par \par \uc2      Shares in Tokyo fell sharply with the benchmark Nikkei \par \par \uc2  average ending below key 16,000 support for the first \par \par \uc2  time since May 1999 as major tech issues were bruised. \par \par \uc2      Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said he was not worried \par \par \uc2  about movements in the Japanese stock market but declined to \par \par \uc2  comment on the Nikkei's drop under 16,000. \par \par \uc2      Economic Planning Minister Taichi Sakaiya, however, said \par \par \uc2  the Bank of Japan should take into account recent falls in \par \par \uc2  stock prices when deciding whether it should end its zero-rate \par \par \uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2      In South Korea, the KOSPI suffered a near five percent drop \par \par \uc2  as foreign selling rocked blue chips SK Telecom and \par \par \uc2  Samsung Electronics . \par \par \uc2      Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to cling to Thursday's gains \par \par \uc2  as players opted to cover their dollar positions ahead of the \par \par \uc2  weekend. \par \par \uc2      SING DOLLAR UPSIDE LIMITED \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar was rescued from 22-month lows after \par \par \uc2  an official from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore said on \par \par \uc2  Thursday it was prepared to allow a gradual appreciation of the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the country's strong fundamentals. \par \par \uc2      It traded comfortably off a 1.7515 trough hit on Monday but \par \par \uc2  analysts said the rebound was not likely to last too long. \par \par \uc2      Chartists said the Sing dollar could breach 1.7300 \par \par \uc2  convincingly next week, with 1.7240 seen as a strong \par \par \uc2  resistance. \par \par \uc2      "In the immediate term, dollar/Sing is going down as charts \par \par \uc2  indicate it's under a downward correction here," said Eric \par \par \uc2  Chong, technical analyst at Standard Chartered in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      "But the recent (dollar/Sing) fall is a bit overdone. \par \par \uc2  Therefore, on a longer term view, the dollar is still on the \par \par \uc2  uptrend," he added. \par \par \uc2      On the fundamental front, any gains will be hampered by \par \par \uc2  lingering political uncertainty in the region, especially ahead \par \par \uc2  of the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) in Indonesia where \par \par \uc2  President Abdurrahman Wahid will be called on to account for \par \par \uc2  his turbulent first year in office. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT BEARISH \par \par \uc2  Despite the Sing dollar's rebound, which has helped other \par \par \uc2  regionals, the embattled Thai baht came under renewed pressure \par \par \uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in case of excess volatility. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand (BOT) deputy governor Tanya Sirivedhin \par \par \uc2  said: "We would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless there were signs that \par \par \uc2  there is really some excessive volatility taking place". \par \par \uc2  The baht erased most of Thursday's gains in early trade as \par \par \uc2  dealers poured cold water on a local press report the BOT had \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in London markets to support it. \par \par \uc2      Bangkok newspaper The Nation said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \par \par \uc2  bought dollars as the baht hit a 10-month low of 41.36. \par \par \uc2      On the sidelines of a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conference in \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Tanya told Reuters she was unaware of any \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as reported by the Nation. \par \par \uc2      "I've been here in Singapore so I don't know if anything \par \par \uc2  like that took place," she said, but added that she would be \par \par \uc2  rather surprised if it had. \par \par \uc2      The baht now looked poised to test the 41.36 level hit on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday as the the authorities seemed to have given a green \par \par \uc2  light for it to weaken further, analysts said. \par \par \uc2      KOREA REFORM \par \par \uc2      Analysts are upbeat on South Korea's economic recovery on \par \par \uc2  the back of strong exports and the booming high-tech sector, \par \par \uc2  but there are still concerns over debt-laden financial firms \par \par \uc2  and slowing restructuring among major conglomerates. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry said it would ask creditors of the \par \par \uc2  country's second largest conglomerate Daewoo Group to \par \par \uc2  draw up final plans by September for reforming or selling off \par \par \uc2  its 12 core affiliates. \par \par \uc2  In a statement issued after a meeting of economic-related \par \par \uc2  ministers, the ministry said creditors would be asked for final \par \par \uc2  reform plans for dozens of non-Daewoo firms also under debt \par \par \uc2  workouts by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  Analysts warned of the risks of slowing reform but pointed \par \par \uc2  out that a possible slowdown in the U.S. economy would prod the \par \par \uc2  government to be more aggressive. \par \par \uc2  "I think there's definitely a reform fatigue going on right \par \par \uc2  now. It's coming through because there's slight amount of \par \par \uc2  complacency due to the fact that the economy is so strong," \par \par \uc2  said Dilip Shahani, senior treasury economist at HSBC Markets \par \par \uc2  in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  "We believe that as the U.S. economy slows down, this \par \par \uc2  reform fatigue will turn into an urgency. As that urgency comes \par \par \uc2  up, the government will be able to push through the final \par \par \uc2  phases," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0936 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     109.12\tab  108.97\tab    -0.14\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7324\tab  1.7335\tab    +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    31.048\tab  31.052\tab    +0.01\par  Korean won   1116.60\tab 1113.30\tab    -0.30\par  Baht\tab      41.24\tab   40.95\tab    -0.70\par  Peso\tab      44.85\tab   44.80\tab    -0.11\par  Rupiah\tab  8930.00\tab 8935.00\tab    +0.06\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.12\tab  102.21\tab    -6.33\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7324\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.95\par  Taiwan dlr    31.048\tab  31.380\tab    +1.07\par  Korean won   1116.60\tab 1135.00\tab    +1.65\par  Baht\tab      41.24\tab   37.45\tab    -9.19\par  Peso\tab      44.85\tab   40.20\tab   -10.37\par  Rupiah\tab  8930.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -21.89\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7997\tab    -0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  AS