\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Early; Singapore Dlr Extends Gains \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2000\par 03:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mixed early Friday, but the Singapore dollar continues to rise after local authorities advocated a stronger exchange rate as a preemptive strike against inflation. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore Thursday said it is prepared to allow a modest appreciation of the local dollar, and gave tacit acknowledgment that it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently to curb weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0120 GMT (9:20 p.m. Thursday EDT), the U.S. dollar is at S$1.7295, down from S$1.7350 late Thursday and S$1.7515 Monday. \par \par \uc2  The rise in the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped lift the rupiah to 8,910 against the dollar from IDR8,963 a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  But the baht and peso opened a touch lower. \par \par \uc2  The dollar in early trade is at THB41.000 from THB40.925 late Thursday and PHP44.980 from PHP44.865, as political uncertainty in Thailand and the Philippines weighed on the respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar is up in early trade, helped by a 1% rise in the local stock market on its open. Taiwan stocks have been falling since April, placing downward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is at NT$31.036 from NT$31.052 previously. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in North Asia, the dollar is at 1,115.3 won, up from KRW1,113.40. \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \