\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Down Late; Baht Near 10-Mo Low \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 763 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2000\par 11:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were lower late Wednesday, as the Thai baht dropped around 1% in intraday trading, hitting its lowest level in almost 10 months. \par \par \uc2  The baht, which has lost more than 2% of its value against the dollar this week, is expected to weaken further after breaking below 41 baht to the dollar, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The baht's relentless slide dragged the Philippine unit below support at the 45 peso-mark against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Caution kept trading volumes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  thin, amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local authorities, dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was slightly higher, while the rupiah was almost 1% weaker. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the New Taiwan dollar was steady, while the South Korean won ended slightly firmer. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's strength against the Japanese yen and a lack of selling pressure in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , apart from profit-taking late in the day, pushed the baht through one support level after another. \par \par \uc2  Around 0859 GMT, the dollar was at THB41.140, up from THB40.925 late Tuesday. The dollar had risen to THB41.340 earlier, its highest level since September 29, 1999. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicated no intention of halting its sharp depreciation. And contrary to expectations, Thai exporters didn't unload their dollars around THB41 and are likely to hold out until the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises to THB41.50, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Panic buying by local importers and stop-loss orders from offshore participants after the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank below support at 41 baht to the dollar contributed to the baht's slide, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also blamed the uncertainty over continuity of economic policies and reform efforts ahead of Thailand's general elections later this year. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's inflation report issued late Tuesday, which confirmed that the country's interest rates will remain depressed for some time, is also expected to keep the baht under pressure, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, the dollar looks set to climb further to its next upside target of THB41.500 as early as Thursday, before heading higher, a dealer at an Asian bank said. \par \par \uc2  "The baht has a target which everyone is looking at now, and that is THB42," says Alison Seng, an analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS International. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso fell to a fresh 30-month low, tracking the Thai baht's fall. The peso is expected to test new post-crisis lows over the next few months, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar pushed through the PHP45 resistance level to close at PHP45.070, up from Tuesday's close of PHP44.755. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had touched an intraday high of PHP45.195 in intraday trade, its highest level since early January 1998, breaking above the 30-month high of PHP44.140 it had hit two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  On the domestic front, concerns that the government will overshoot its budget deficit target this year and the country's sluggish economic growth continued to unnerve investors, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers said. \par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered Bank expects the peso to decline further to PHP46 by the end of the third quarter, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Steve Brice said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar-selling by Indonesian state banks and profit-taking in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by offshore participants had recouped part of the rupiah's losses, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had climbed to as high as IDR9,150 in early trading, but retreated to IDR9,070 around 0905 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Similarly, steady U.S. dollar selling in Singapore by local banks - which traders said might have been executed on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore - helped the Singapore dollar to recover, resisting the pressure from its Southeast Asian counterparts. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was at S$1.7428, down from S$1.7452 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also present in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, albeit in a relatively more overt manner, selling around US$200 million Wednesday to stabilize the New Taiwan dollar, dealers said. A rebound in the local stock market also buoyed Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended at NT$31.061, barely changed from NT$31.063 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won edged up as local banks liquidated their long-dollar positions following the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength earlier in the day, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 1,115.30 won, down slightly from Tuesday's close of KRW1,115.60. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7q03lsy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoa