\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Slightly Up Early Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2000\par 05:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is slightly higher early Wednesday due to U.S. dollar selling amid fears that \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0244 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7448, down from S$1.7452 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said offers by local names have weighed on the U.S. dollar since the start of the local session, and market participants remain wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. dollar is supported by buying interest around S$1.7430 and remains capped by offers around S$1.7455-S$1.7460. \par \par \uc2  Despite its rise against the Indonesian rupiah and the Thai baht, market participants are reluctant to push the U.S \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher as many are still smarting from late Monday's suspected MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the U.S. dollar hit a 22-month high of S$1.7515, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They expect the U.S. dollar to trade in a tight S$1.7430-S$1.7470 range Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's United Overseas Bank Group said Wednesday it will continue to sell U.S. dollars on upticks toward S$1.7500 unless it rises above Y110, 41.50 baht or breaches 9,500 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4809; amit.prakash@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7q03kxx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
