\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Early; Baht At Near 10-Mo Low \b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2000\par 03:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mixed early Wednesday, with the Thai baht extending its fall to sink below the psychologically-important 41 baht mark to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The baht's slide to its lowest level in almost 10 months has dented the Philippine peso. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has also moved lower after finding its way again below IDR9,000 support late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar, however, largely resisted the downward pressure from its Southeast Asian counterparts as investors remained spooked following Monday's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In North Asia, the New Taiwan dollar is steady, while the South Korean won is firmer. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the dollar has climbed to its highest level since Sept. 30, 1999, to hit THB41.075 around 0115 GMT (9:15 p.m. EDT Tuesday), up from THB40.925 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's inflation report issued late Tuesday, which confirmed that the country's interest rates will remain low for some time, is expected to keep the near-term baht outlook weak, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand said Tuesday that baht weakness might push core inflation above a target range of 0 to 3.5%, but noted that the authorities have the option of allowing the baht to continue to fall, rather than meddling with a low interest rate policy designed to support a fragile recovery. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is likely to remain capped at THB41.100 in the short term unless the dollar rises above Y109.30 vis-a-vis the yen, a dealer at a U.S. bank said. The dollar will likely face support around THB40.800. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah continued to slide on pent-up offshore demand for dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Contributing to the rupiah's weakness were remarks by chief economics minister Kwik Kian Gie Tuesday that the government may scrap debt-settlement agreements signed with a number of Indonesia's top business groups, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 9,076 rupiah, up slightly from IDR9,025 late Tuesday. It is expected to be capped around IDR9,150 Wednesday amid expectations state banks might support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around that level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In Manila, the dollar was at 44.910 pesos, up from Tuesday's close of PHP44.755. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at S$1.7451, barely changed from S$1.7452 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In South Korea, the dollar was at 1,115.0 won, down slightly from Tuesday's close of KRW1,115.60 on month-end dollar-selling by local exporters and mild profit-taking in dollar positions by local banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at NT$31.060, little changed from Tuesday's close of NT$31.063, as the local stock market recovered early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807;\par netty.ismail@dowjones.com\par -0- 26/07/00 01-48G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7q03kus\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
