\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Down Late; Thai Baht Hits Fresh 9-Mo Low \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 782 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2000\par 10:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were weaker late Tuesday, as the Thai baht continued its downward spiral to hit fresh nine-month lows. \par \par \uc2  The poor sentiment on the baht, which is expected to slide further, weighed on the other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In North Asia, a slump in their respective local stock markets dented the New Taiwan dollar and the South Korean won. \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also adjusting to the U.S. dollar's strength against the yen, which had again tested the Y109 support level to the dollar Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The baht - the latest target for investors already bearish on most Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - fell to its lowest level since Oct. 1, 1999, when it tested the psychologically-important support level of 41.000 baht to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In late Asian trading, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was traded at THB41.000 in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokers, and was bid at that level by some participants in the Singapore interbank market. However, offshore profit-taking and dollar-selling by exporters limited the dollar's strength. \par \par \uc2  Around 0750 GMT (3:50 a.m. EDT), the dollar was at THB40.925, up from THB40.805 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The baht is down 5.8% against the dollar since early June amid uncertainty over the continuity of economic policies and reform efforts ahead of Thailand's general elections later this year. The weakness in Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets has also hurt the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  This week technical and option-related dollar-selling, the depressed stock market and local dollar demand by importers and debtors have triggered the baht's sharper-than-expected decline, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's apparent tolerance over the baht's weakness gave investors the added impetus to push the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. \par \par \uc2  Deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pakorn Malakul reiterated Tuesday that the baht's fall is due mainly to the U.S. dollar's rise against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that it hasn't seen any unreasonably speculative or abnormal activity in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts expect more gloom for the baht in the short term. \par \par \uc2  "I really don't think we have seen the worst," said Syetarn Hansakul, treasury economist at WestLB Research. "With the next week or so, it can go in the direction of THB42.00 (to the dollar)." \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah was jolted out of its narrow trading range after President Abdurrahman Wahid abruptly canceled a news conference he was scheduled to give late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar climbed above the psychologically-important 9,000 rupiah level to trade at IDR9,025 around 0920 GMT, up from IDR8,903 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Lingering uncertainty over Wahid's political fate ahead of Indonesia's national assembly meeting next month had also prompted some offshore participants to start building up long-dollar positions again. Sentiment, however, remained cautious amid fears Bank Indonesia would defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Many traders expect strong dollar demand to emerge around IDR8,800 to IDR8,850, but fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely cap the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around IDR9,200 in the short term. \par \par \uc2  The bleak outlook for the baht and the rupiah stung the Philippine peso. The dollar was at 44.750 pesos, up from Monday's close of PHP44.60. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was slightly weaker, as the pressure from the strength of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was offset by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Market participants were wary of pushing the Singapore dollar lower, following the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the U.S. dollar down from its brief rise to a 22-month high of S$1.7515. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was at S$1.7452, up marginally from S$1.7441 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  In South Korea, the dollar finished at 1,115.60 won, up from Monday's close of KRW1,114. \par \par \uc2  Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at NT$31.063, up from NT$30.046 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The fall in the local stock markets had hurt the South Korean and Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Investors are, meanwhile, awaiting U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's testimony on monetary policy later Tuesday to the House Banking Committee. His speech isn't expected to be different from the version he delivered to a Senate panel last week. However, investors are keeping a close watch on other comments that could emerge in response to questions posed from the House panel following his address. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7p03m4w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
