\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Down Late; Baht Skids To 9-Mo Low \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 954 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2000\par 10:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were weaker late Monday, with the Thai baht skidding to its lowest level in more than nine months and casting a pall on most other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was largely stable as the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  took a backseat following last week's roller-coaster ride when President Abdurrahman Wahid refused to explain to Parliament the reasons for the sacking of two ministers. /// \par \par \uc2  ///The Philippine peso and the Singapore dollar were also down late Monday. \par \par \uc2  In North Asia, sharp losses on the local stock markets hammered the South Korean won and the New Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht was pushed to its weakest level since Oct. 1, 1999, partly due to a 3.6% slide in the key index on the Thai stock market to below the psychologically-important 300 mark. \par \par \uc2  Around 0810 GMT (4:10 a.m. EDT), the dollar was at 40.805 baht, up from THB40.315 in Asian trading last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Stop-loss dollar buying by U.S. banks that were caught short after they failed to depress the dollar around the 40.400 baht level provided more impetus to the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's descent, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The expiry of substantial options Friday at a strike price of THB40.700 to the dollar had also fueled concerns that the baht could be pressured further, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, a dealer at a Thai bank said the dollar will likely face resistance around THB40.800 to THB40.850 in the short term. \par \par \uc2  Signaling that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely stay on the sidelines Monday, Thai Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda said the baht's decline against the U.S. dollar Monday was line with weakness in the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Investors, meanwhile, shrugged off the results of the election for a new governor of Bangkok, which was viewed by some observers as favorable for the ruling Democrat Party ahead of the general elections to be held later this year. \par \par \uc2  The results represented a setback for Thailand's newest political party, Thai Rak Thai, whose candidate lost out to one a medium-sized party, Pracharkorn Thai (Thai Citizens') Party, by a landslide margin. Thai Rak Thai Party is perceived as the closest rival to the Democrat Party as a leader of the next coalition government. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, Rebecca Patterson, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan\par (Singapore), said the election results shouldn't affect the baht: "It's\par not a factor at all."\par - - 24/07/00 08-56G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar succumbed to the baht's weakness, but rapidly\par rebounded on suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  late in the day by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which declined to comment as expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar clawed its way up to S$1.7515, its highest level since\par Sept. 4, 1998, before provoking aggressive selling in the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par by a local bank, which usually acts as an agent for the de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Around 0945 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7441, down from S$1.7469\par late Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso wasn't spared either by the baht's tumble.\par Additionally, worries over domestic security, as riot police clubbed\par protesters ahead of President Joseph Estrada's state of the nation\par address amid waning confidence in his administration, and over the\par ballooning budget deficit, continued to roil the Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite adhering to a targeted budget deficit of PHP62.5 billion for\par this year, the government has proposed a wider deficit of PHP85 billion\par for 2001. Next year's deficit, if approved, would be wider than PHP15.5\par billion deficit originally planned for 2001 under the government's\par medium-term development plan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar closed at 44.600 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up\par from Friday's close of PHP44.400, and is set to re-test its recent high\par of PHP45.15 in the short term, analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah was steady at 8,903 rupiah to the dollar,\par following President Wahid's apology last Friday to parliament.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In his second written statement delivered to parliament, Wahid\par expressed regret about recent events and offered a more conciliatory\par explanation of why he didn't feel constitutionally bound to answer\par parliamentarians' questions over his sacking of two ministers earlier\par this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Doubts, however, prevail that Wahid's attempt to pacify angry\par legislators will ease the political tension ahead of the country's\par national assembly next month, market observers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Patterson at JP Morgan said while the rupiah is expected to be\par volatile in the next two to three weeks, it will likely be supported by\par Bank Indonesia's moves to defend the beleaguered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and fears of\par such \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , even if it doesn't step in.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah will likely, however, weaken toward IDR10,000 to the dollar\par at the end of the third quarter after the national assembly meeting,\par even if Wahid survives the session, the strategist added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investors will likely continue to shun the country given the\par social and political instability there, the slow privatization process\par and the patchy economic recovery, she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In North Asia, foreign equity outflows, which led to sharp losses in\par local stock prices, eroded the South Korean won and the New Taiwan\par dollar, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Seoul, the dollar finished at 1,114 won, up from Friday's close of\par KRW1,112.70.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ended at NT$31.046,\par up slightly from NT$31.019 late Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807;\par netty.ismail@dowjones.com\par -0- 24/07/00 10-25G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7o03k3h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
