\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late On Volatile Rupiah, Weak Trade Data \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2000\par 11:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was slightly lower late Thursday, following a volatile Indonesian rupiah and the issuing of weaker-than-expected June trade data, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0924 GMT (5:24 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7460, up from S$1.7443 late Wednesday in Asia, but down from S$1.7475 earlier Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Indonesian President Abdurrahman Wahid's refusal Thursday to answer questions in parliament on why he fired two cabinet members earlier this year lifted the U.S. dollar above 9,200 rupiah, but it has since retreated to IDR8,880 on rumored dollar-selling by state-run banks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah's rise above IDR8,750 to the U.S. dollar could prompt large scale selling of U.S. dollars for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The consensus forecast of analysts surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires was for a 15% on year rise in non-oil exports in June. \par \par \uc2  Subsequent remarks by a top trade official that Singapore isn't relying on a favorable exchange rate for export growth helped lift the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above the day's lows, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The rupiah is back to where it was earlier today, so I'm surprised that the (U.S. dollar) is looking so bid (against the Singapore dollar)," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  A second dealer said that profit-taking and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to cap the U.S. dollar's potential rise between S$1.7460-S$1.7470 in the near term. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely be supported by demand from local companies below S$1.7430. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah, however, remains the key influence on the Singapore dollar. Its rise above IDR8,750 to a U.S. dollar prompted a large scale selling of U.S. dollars for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4809; amit.prakash@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (Corrected 0949GMT) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah's rise above IDR8,750 to the U.S. dollar could prompt large scale selling of U.S. dollars for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (In an item timed 0926 GMT, it was misstated that large scale selling of U.S. dollars had occurred.) \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7k03jfw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
