\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Exports Not Boosted By Exch Rate - Trade  Executive \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2000\par 08:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Singapore isn't relying on a favorable exchange rate for export growth, Barry Desker, chief executive officer of the Trade Development Board, said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Our export growth is driven by the upturn in global demand and healthy economic growth in Asia," said Desker, who spoke at a news conference following the release of June export data. \par \par \uc2  Non-oil domestic exports grew at an annual rate of just 10.5%, far lower than the consensus forecast of 15% and down from a growth of 15.6% in May. \par \par \uc2  Desker said that growth of non-oil domestic exports is expected to moderate in the second half of the year given the higher base in the comparable period of 1999. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar is at its weakest level against the U.S. dollar since September 1998. Despite strong economic fundamentals, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been sapped by weakness in the Indonesian rupiah and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in recent weeks to support the level of the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, economists have said the MAS is in no hurry to see a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given that inflation is well under control. \par \par \uc2  Around 0655 GMT (2:55 a.m EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at around S$1.7465, up from S$1.7443 late Wednesday in Asia. At the end of 1999, the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.6650 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amit Prakash; Dow Jones Newswires; (65) 421-4809;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par -0- 20/07/00 07-22G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7k03j79\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
