\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Early; Singapore Dlr Finds Respite \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2000\par 03:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mixed early Tuesday, with the U.S. dollar's rise against its \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  counterpart capped by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  After having allowed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drift lower in recent weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore - which rarely comments on its actions - was rumored to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around S$1.7485 late Monday, after the U.S. dollar rose to as high as S$1.7490, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, the U.S. dollar remains well supported as investors buy on the dip, especially around S$1.7450, dealers said. But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise will likely be tempered by fears of another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they added. \par \par \uc2  Around 0110 GMT (9:10 p.m. EDT Monday), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7477, down from levels before the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the MAS but steady from levels following the move. \par \par \uc2  Anticipated further weakness in the Indonesian rupiah is expected to exert downward pressure on the Singapore dollar and other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is stable at 9,515 rupiah to the dollar, but could weaken ahead of an expected showdown between President Abdurrahman Wahid and the Indonesian parliament Thursday over his controversial sacking of two ministers earlier this year, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht has been weighed on by dollar-buying by local corporates, who returned to the market after a national holiday Monday to find the baht having already been pushed down by offshore players to 40.300 baht to the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Thai exporters are, meanwhile, selling dollars around current levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is at THB40.340, up from THB40.225 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  In Manila, the dollar is at 44.680 pesos, up from Monday's close of PHP44.590. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar is being pressured by the 0.8% slide Tuesday in the local stock market, dealers said. The U.S. dollar is at NT$30.939, up from Monday's close of NT$30.912. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won is slightly lower, amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the local authorities, after the government warned last Friday it was willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the won from appreciating too sharply, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 1,113.10 won, up from Friday's close of KRW1,112.90. The South Korean market was closed Monday for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807;\par netty.ismail@dowjones.com\par -0- 18/07/00 01-27G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7i03h5f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
