\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Early; Rupiah Slide Sparks US Dlr Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2000\par 04:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is lower early Monday, falling below a key psychological resistance level amid U.S. dollar buying by European and U.S. names in response to the Indonesian rupiah's weakness, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0155 GMT (9:55 p.m. EDT Sunday), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7460, up from S$1.7407 late Friday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Against the rupiah, the U.S. dollar was at IDR9,546, up from IDR 9,473 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  has encouraged market participants to push the U.S. dollar above the S$1.7450 psychological resistance. But they remain wary of swift action by the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Most of the early U.S. dollar buying has been to fulfill customers orders, but some participants have also been covering short positions in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  While the rupiah is expected to continue influencing the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market participants will also be watching yen moves after the Bank of Japan's policy board meeting later Monday. \par \par \uc2  "People want to know if they (BoJ) will hike rates," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the U.S. dollar to mostly trade in a S$1.7430-S$1.7470 range Monday. U.S. dollars buying is expected on dips, with selling likely to emerge above S$1.7470 on fears of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they added. \par \par \uc2  -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (65) 421-4809; amit.prakash@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7h03feu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
