\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Down Early; Dlr Above IDR9,500 \b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2000\par 03:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mostly weaker early Monday, as the Indonesian rupiah slips below the psychologically important IDR9,500 support level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0131 GMT (9:31 p.m. EDT Sunday), the U.S. dollar has advanced to IDR9,575, up from IDR9,461 late Friday. The rise comes amid nervousness ahead of Thursday's showdown between President Abdurrahman Wahid and the Indonesian parliament over his controversial sacking of two ministers earlier this year, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "This may provide a volatile week ahead," a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  Resistance for the dollar around IDR9,575 is, however, expected to remain strong as state banks will likely sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and offshore investors could lock in profits around this level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's slide has prompted European names to push the Singapore dollar below the S$1.7450 psychological support level, with no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it did when the U.S. dollar last week rose above S$1.7400, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar has climbed to S$1.7457, up from S$1.7425 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Investors are keeping a close watch on whether the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could now test the key S$1.7500 mark. \par \par \uc2  With the Thai market closed for a national holiday, offshore players have dragged the baht lower. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has risen to 40.145 baht, up from THB40.025 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  In Manila, the region's weakness has weighed on the peso. The dollar was at 44.520 pesos, up from PHP44.495 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Although the yen has had little impact on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently, investors are keeping a close watch on whether the Bank of Japan will end its 17-month-long zero interest rate policy later in the day when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy board meets. \par \par \uc2  The direction of the yen following the Bank of Japan's decision could have an impact on the Singapore dollar and the New Taiwan dollar later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely react indifferently to the decision, as trading will more likely be dictated by domestic political and economic concerns, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  South Korea is closed for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807;\par netty.ismail@dowjones.com\par -0- 17/07/00 01-32G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7h03fcx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
