\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late; Rupiah Set To Tumble Further \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2000\par 11:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed late Wednesday, with the Indonesian rupiah plummeting to a 21-month intraday low against the dollar before recovering some of its losses. \par \par \uc2  After pressuring the Philippine, Thai and Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  through key support levels earlier this week, investors preyed on the rupiah on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar pierced through the psychologically important 9,500 rupiah mark in afternoon dealings, climbing as high as IDR9,505, its highest intraday level since mid-March, 1999. The last time the dollar was above IDR9,500 at the close of Asian trading hours was in October, 1998. \par \par \uc2  Panic dollar buying by local corporates that needed to service foreign debt obligations and persisting doubts over President Abdurrahman Wahid's hold on power and economic reforms cast a pall on the rupiah, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers said. \par \par \uc2  A local newspaper report quoting Bank Indonesia acting governor, Anwar Nasution, as suggesting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was largely powerless in halting the rupiah's slide also contributed to the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar failed to convincingly breach above IDR9,500 as dollar profit-taking by offshore players set in. \par \par \uc2  Market talk that the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has invited foreign treasury heads for a meeting Thursday, fueling speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be considering ways to strengthen the rupiah, in part helped recoup some of the rupiah's losses, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0915 GMT, the dollar was at IDR9,420, up from IDR9,338 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Market pundits are betting that the dollar will likely march higher toward IDR10,000 over the coming week on speculative buying interest. \par \par \uc2  "IDR9,700 to IDR9,800 will be the next crucial area," said Steve Brice, strategist at Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar strengthened in late trading but remained below S$1.7400 after tracking the Indonesian rupiah, dealers said. Fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the U.S. dollar climbed to around S$1.7440 fueled profit-taking in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they added. \par \par \uc2  Around 1000 GMT, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at S$1.7413, down from S$1.7433 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  After sinking below THB40 against the dollar Tuesday, the Thai baht remained depressed below that level after the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor gave the green light for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken further, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul said Wednesday that the recent baht weakness has been in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and added that it is in an appropriate range relative to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Thailand's export competitors. He said there was no need for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the baht for the time being. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at THB40.085 late Wednesday in Asia, up slightly from THB40.045 the previous day. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso rebounded slightly, thanks to dollar profit-taking by offshore players after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched an intraday high of PHP45.095, dealers said. The dollar Tuesday hit a 30-month high of PHP45.150. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at PHP44.640 Wednesday in the Phlippine Dealing System, down from Tuesday's close at PHP44.820. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the South Korean won ended Seoul trading higher as foreign investors bought the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to invest in the local stock market, and as Tuesday's bank strike ended after the government hammered out a compromise with the bank union, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 1,115.60 won, down from Tuesday's KRW1,116.50 in thin trading. Traders said they expect the dollar to trade in the KRW1,113 to KRW1,116 range Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A 1.2% slide in the Taiwan stock market weighed on the New Taiwan dollar, dealers said. The U.S. dollar closed at NT$30.862, up from NT$30.842 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7c03emf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
