\par\par \b \uc2  Sing dollar breaks key support, falls limited. \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2000\par 07:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 11 (Reuters) - The faltering Singapore dollar broke key psychological support to hit 16-month lows on Tuesday as analysts predicted more declines in the weeks ahead. \par \par \uc2  In early trade, the Sing dollar, which has recently hovered in a tight range, breached 1.7400, a level that had been widely expected to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  intevention to curb further falls. \par \par \uc2  "There's a lot of talk, certainly technically, that 1.74 is a very key level," said Steve Brice, treasury economist at Standard Chartered. "That's why the authorities have been protective about levels..." \par \par \uc2  But despite the breach of key support and heightened speculation, there have been no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against an undisclosed trade-weighted basket. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Sing dollar now looked poised to test the next key target at 1.7500 as the MAS was probably not too concerned with the recent softness. \par \par \uc2  The fall was mostly due to weakness in other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , battered due to domestic political and economic uncertainty, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "We would have to ask the Thais, the Filipinos, the Indonesians. Primarily, it is really those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which are directing the Sing dollar at this point," said Song Seng Wun, regional economist at G.K. Goh Research. \par \par \uc2  But players saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gradually stabilising given healthy economic fundamentals coupled with low inflation. \par \par \uc2  "Clearly with the economic growth here, there's nothing to be massively fuelling the weaker Sing," said Kevin Ralph, first vice president of strategic trading at Sanwa Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's second quarter gross domestic product data, released on Monday, pointed to a stronger-than-expected 7.7 percent growth in the second quarter compared to the same period the previous year. \par \par \uc2  ((Yonggi Kang, Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk +65-870-3925 \par \par \uc2  e-mail: yonggi.kang@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw7b01uma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
