\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Crosses 1.7400 Vs USD \b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2000\par 03:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar has fallen below the psychologically-important S$1.7400 level against its U.S. counterpart early Tuesday, as players cautiously bid up the U.S. dollar with no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Around 0115 GMT (9:15 p.m. EDT Monday), the U.S. dollar was at\par S$1.7409, up from S$1.7385 late Monday. The last time the U.S. dollar\par was trading above S$1.7400 was September 10, 1998.\par - - 11/07/00 01-25G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is poised to face stiff resistance around S$1.7450, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the U.S. dollar touched S$1.7280 - the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level about two weeks ago - had encouraged market participants to gradually push up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  With the sharp depreciation in the Indonesian rupiah, the Thai baht and the Philippine peso over the past week, the MAS is probably more tolerant of the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, market participants remained guarded amid fears the MAS may step in "if there's any sign of renewed aggressive buying" in the U.S. dollar versus the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a chief dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 6