\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late On Stronger Rupiah; Active Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2000\par 11:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Gyrating in step with a stronger Indonesian rupiah, the Singapore dollar was higher against the U.S. dollar late Thursday amid active two-way trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0805 GMT (4:00 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7360, down from S$1.7370 late Wednesday in Asia. Against the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar was trading at 9,250 rupiah late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose briefly above last week's high of S$1.7380. However, a rebound in the rupiah to IDR9,190 to the dollar, from a 16-month low Wednesday of IDR9,395 helped push the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar higher. \par \par \uc2  Coupled with fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the U.S. unit was pushed to an intraday low of S$1.7348. \par \par \uc2  "The market is respecting the previous high and is not likely to take the (U.S. dollar) above that (level) unless it shoots over 9,400 rupiah," said a European bank dealer in Singapore. There has been buying and selling of U.S. dollars for Singapore dollars through Thursday, he added///./// \par \par \uc2  Political tension between Indonesian President Aburrahman Wahid and the parliament and a bomb explosion at the Indonesian attorney general's office have weakened the rupiah this week. It hit an intraday low of IDR9,450 Wednesday, after two more bombs were discovered at the prosecutor's office. \par \par \uc2  Another trader said that after three days of the dollar's rise against Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some market participants likely took profit by liquidating long U.S. dollar positions against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adding to the latter's strength. \par \par \uc2  However, the U.S. dollar is well supported at S$1.7330, with fears of MAS action capping it around S$1.7380, he added. \par \par \uc2  The European bank dealer said the rupiah would continue to dictate the Singapore dollar's tone over the next few days. \par \par \uc2  "It (rupiah) is basically politically driven, so the risk (to the Singapore dollar) is on the upside," the European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Thursday, a Standard Chartered Bank research note said that the MAS is likely to allow the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to break above S$1.7400 if the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness continues. \par \par \uc2  -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4807; amit.prakash@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7603apw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
