\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Follows Rupiah Up Early; Tight Range Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2000\par 04:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is higher early Thursday, mimicking a stronger rupiah, and is expected to trade in a narrow range through the day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0230 GMT (10:30 p.m. EDT Wednesday), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7359, down from S$1.7370 late Wednesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened higher, surging to a high of S$1.7381 before a rebound in the rupiah pushed it to a low of S$1.7348. Dealers said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah rebounded to IDR9,190 to a dollar after closing at a 16-month low Wednesday at IDR9,395. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah had hit an intraday low of IDR9,450 to the dollar Wednesday after a bomb was found at the office of Indonesia's attorney general, a day after an explosion ripped through the building. \par \par \uc2  Political tension between Indonesian President Aburrahman Wahid and the parliament has also weakened the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the Singapore dollar to continue moving in tandem with the rupiah and other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that it's likely to trade in a narrow range of S$1.7340 to $1.7380 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is well supported at S$1.7320-S$1.7330 and will face initial resistance at S$1.7380-S$1.7390 followed by much stronger resistance at S$1.7400, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, Standard Chartered bank said in a research note that the MAS is likely to allow the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to break above S$1.7400 if regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness continues. \par \par \uc2  -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4807; amit.prakash@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7603agv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
