\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Slightly Weaker Early In Thin Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2000\par 05:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is slightly weaker early Tuesday in light trading, but fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should keep it from drifting much lower, dealers said \par \par \uc2  Around 0238 GMT (10:38 p.m. EDT Monday), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7327, up from S$1.7317 late Monday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said market participants are reluctant to push the U.S. dollar above S$1.7330, the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday. \par \par \uc2  "That is a key resistance because a lot of people burned their fingers last week," a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  Also, there is little reason to expect market participants to buy U.S. dollars aggressively because many are already long on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added. "Yesterday, the market was short on (U.S.) dollars." \par \par \uc2  According to dealers, the Singapore dollar market is still focusing on the Indonesian rupiah and the Thai baht, but has largely ignored the ignored the weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  Early Tuesday, the Indonesian rupiah reached a 16-month low against the dollar, hitting 9,000 rupiah in a Singapore-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broker, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The announcement of a 0330 GMT news conference by Indonesian President Abdurrahman Wahid on an unspecified subject is unnerving markets, and may have sparked the brief trade at IDR9,000, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Thai political uncertainty and the weaker rupiah are likely to push the U.S. dollar to test a year-high of 39.47 baht. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the Singapore dollar to trade in a S$1.7290-$1.7330 range Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4807; amit.prakash@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw74037nf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
