\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Midday On Weaker Rupiah; Thin Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2000\par 06:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is slightly weaker midday Monday, tracking a weaker Indonesian rupiah in thin trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0414 GMT (12:14 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7290, up from S$1.7271 late Friday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the local unit is expected to move in a very tight range, with fears of another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowing its decline. \par \par \uc2  According to dealers, the MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York trading hours Thursday after the U.S. dollar shot up to S$1.7380. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again sold U.S. dollars for Singapore dollars late Friday morning at $1.7330, they added. \par \par \uc2  "The focus is on the rupiah, which is weaker on political uncertainty and the Sing (Singapore dollar) is reflecting that," a dealer at a European bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell midmorning Monday to its lowest level against the U.S. dollar since last September on offshore selling linked to President Abdurrahman Wahid's talk of a crackdown on opponents suspected of inciting riots. \par \par \uc2  At 0413 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at 8,850 rupiah, up from IDR8,725 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said market participants were surprised by last week's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  still remain weak against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank in Singapore said the rupiah is expected to further weaken to IDR9,000 to the U.S. dollar this week, and is expected to pressure the Singapore unit to drift lower. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the U.S. dollar to trade in a S$1.7260-S$1.7320 range Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4807;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par -0- 03/07/00 04-26G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw73038ov\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
