\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Early; S$ Resists Rupiah Pressure \b0\par\par\uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2000\par 03:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mixed early Friday, with the Singapore dollar resisting downward pressure from the Indonesian rupiah's weakness amid unconfirmed talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in overnight trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The MAS - which doesn't usually comment on its moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - was said to have sold U.S. dollars when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  climbed to a high of S$1.7380 in overnight trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's sharp weakness was attributed to technical stop-loss orders, which were triggered when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  muscled its way through S$1.7360, a resistance level that had proved difficult break in recent weeks due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  With no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar advanced to $1.7380, but retreated quickly amid talk that MAS had moved to defended the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around that level. \par \par \uc2  Around 0115 GMT (9:15 p.m. EDT Thursday), the U.S. dollar was traded at S$1.7333, down from S$1.7344 in late Asia trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to trade between S$1.7320 and S$1.7380 for the rest of the day, a chief dealer at a European bank said. But a Japanese bank dealer said fears of another MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could cap the U.S. unit around S$1.7350. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah is poised to weaken further to IDR8,800 to a U.S. dollar, after sinking below IDR8,700 support Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Strong corporate dollar demand to meet debt repayment schedules had weighed on the rupiah, prompting some dollar short-covering in London and New York trading Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0135 GMT, the dollar was traded at IDR8,750, up from IDR8,735 late Thursday in Asia. The dollar had tested IDR8,760 resistance earlier Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said if the dollar soars to IDR9,000, it could spark a nervous selloff in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the Philippines, tight liquidity dented the peso, which is trading at PHP43.235 to a dollar, compared with Thursday's close at PHP43.170. The dollar faces resistance around PHP43.250, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has slipped to NT$30.804, from Thursday's close at NT$30.808, due to exporter demand for the local unit, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In South Korea, the dollar has edged up to 1,115.70 won, from Thursday's close at KRW1,114.90, on short-covering in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local banks, dealers said. The dollar may, however, lose its strength because local exporters are expected to continue to sell the U.S. unit to pay for month-end expenses, they added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is set trade in KRW1,113-KRW1,116 range Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the dollar was steady around THB39.175, compared with THB39.165 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6u0384n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\