\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore MAS Action Not Expected To Signal Policy Shift \b0\par\par\uc2 778 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2000\par 12:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by apparently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the move didn't signal a fundamental shift in policy, analysts and traders said Friday. \par \par \uc2  The suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started late Thursday in New York trading hours and then continued early Friday morning in Asia, pushing the Singapore dollar to its strongest level in two weeks against its U.S. counterpart. \par \par \uc2  Late Friday in Asia, the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7277, down sharply from its overnight peak of S$1.7380 and Thursday's Asian close of S$1.7344. \par \par \uc2  The move likely was a signal that the MAS wouldn't tolerate a sharply weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than a fundamental shift away from its neutral monetary policy stance, which is meant to encourage non-inflationary growth, economists and traders said. \par \par \uc2  The MAS declined to comment. "As a policy we don't usually comment," a spokeswoman for the MAS said. \par \par \uc2  The purpose of the MAS action, said a strategist at a European bank, is "not to try to change the trend but to create an awareness of where the tolerance levels are." \par \par \uc2  In recent months, the MAS has maintained a neutral policy on the Singapore dollar, meaning that it wants the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain stable against a basket of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its biggest trading partners. \par \par \uc2  With the help of a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and an inflation rate that remains low, the MAS can continue to nurture Singapore's export-led economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  A tighter policy - meaning a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - could derail the recovery, while a looser policy could spark inflation by raising the price of imported goods. \par \par \uc2  Although the Singapore dollar, like other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the world, has weakened against the U.S. dollar, it has gained against the euro and some of the other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that make up the basket, economists said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par            Surging US Dlr Creates Dilemma For MAS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the surging U.S. dollar has created a dilemma for the MAS,\par economists added. With interest rates low in Singapore and high in the\par U.S., it has become easy to make money by borrowing Singapore dollars\par and selling them for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Investors who made such bets were protected from losses by the MAS's\par policy of keeping the Singapore dollar from weakening too much.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Clearly, the temptation is to buy (U.S.) dollars against Sing given\par that you've got the MAS protecting your downside," said the European\par bank strategist.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The accumulation of long U.S. dollar positions threatened to overwhelm\par the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , pushing the U.S. dollar beyond what some\par observers say is a key technical level of S$1.7400.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That represents the U.S. dollar's last peak against the Singapore\par dollar in March 1999. Technical analysis suggests that pushed beyond\par that level, the U.S. dollar would quickly shoot up to the previous peak\par of S$1.7900, said Steve Brice, Treasury economist at Standard Chartered\par Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It would be a key signal to the market that they are willing to let\par the Sing weaken against the (U.S.) dollar," Brice said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the apparent MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't signal a shift in policy,\par it has prompted renewed speculation as to where the Singapore dollar is\par likely to head from here.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Several traders said the U.S. dollar is likely to weaken further in\par coming days as long positions are liquidated. But they add that the U.S.\par dollar will find support at about S$1.7220 and then resume its ascent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar will weaken as the interest-rate differential\par with the U.S. continues to widen and the Indonesian rupiah weakens\par further in response to political uncertainty in Jakarta, some analysts\par argue.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Continued investment abroad by big Singapore companies could also add\par to the downward pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as money flows out of the\par country. Some traders cited as a possible factor reports that two\par Singapore banks are in the running to buy the Hong Kong assets of Chase\par Manhattan Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the other hand, the euro's sharp recovery in the past two days\par could be a signal that the U.S. dollar's glory days are over, and\par therefore cap its gains against the Singapore dollar, said David\par Simmonds, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Citibank in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The rally of the euro tends to put a little bit of a ceiling" on\par expectations that the U.S. dollar will rise to S$1.7400 or beyond,\par Simmonds said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Christopher Wellisz, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4802;\par christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6u036ki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
