\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Sit tight ahead of FOMC outcome. \b0\par\par\uc2 849 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2000\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 28 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed \par \par \uc2  rangebound late on Wednesday as players found no compelling \par \par \uc2  reasons to take fresh positions ahead of the Federal Open \par \par \uc2  Market Committee's interest rates decision later in the day. \par \par \uc2      Although most analysts expected the Fed to forego another \par \par \uc2  increase this time, the market was likely to watch closely what \par \par \uc2  the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would say about the economy. \par \par \uc2      The baht gained lost ground after an opposition's party's \par \par \uc2  move to destabilise the government barely created political \par \par \uc2  ripples. \par \par \uc2      The Thai opposition New Aspiration Party (NAP) had \par \par \uc2  threatened to resign en masse in a bid to hasten a general \par \par \uc2  election, but only 50 out of 116 members of parliments tendered \par \par \uc2  resignation on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      Meanwhile, rating agency Moody's Investor Service said \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's rating could be upgraded this year but there was no \par \par \uc2  guarantee it would be. It has had positive outlook on \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ceiling since October last year. \par \par \uc2      The yen (JPY=) retreated to 105.60 level as the market \par \par \uc2  braced for the Fed's verdict on interest rates and Japan's \par \par \uc2  quarterly business sentiment survey next week. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab    -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won ticked higher on demand from exporters and foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par funds seeking to invest in local stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreigners were net buyers of 180 billion won worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local stocks and some $130 million was converted into the local\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday to settle previous foreign stock buying,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the macro front, the country produced a $1.54 current\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par account surplus in May compared with a deficit of $298 million\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Although the surplus was the biggest in six months, it was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a sharp drop from $2.29 billion in May last year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was weaker, barely drawing support from yet\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par another rate hike by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank Indonesia on Wednesday increased the benchmark\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rate on its one-month paper to above 12 percent to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shore up the battered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The weekly auction of one-month SBI certificates resulted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in a weighted average interest rate of 12.33 percent against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 11.74 percent last week. The rate now stands at its highest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level since December 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso slipped further despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par governor's comment that Tuesday's fall was just temporary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The local unit broke the key 43 to the dollar psychological\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support on Tuesday and failed to crawl back throughout the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The 43.20 per dollar level is likely to be tested soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael Buenaventura, who\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par is in Paris, said late on Tuesday the slide was partly caused\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by window-dressing for quarter-end positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "This is only temporary. There is nervousness also in what\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Fed would do a few hours from now," Buenaventura said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On Wednesday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deputy governor Amando Tetangco\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said on Wednesday dollar supply was not sufficient to meet\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Political unrest at home in the past few months has hurt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the peso and beefed up demand for the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar was a touch lower with the market still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par feeling the effects of hefty \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par previous day.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been detected by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers in the previous two sessions as weak stocks and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seasonal U.S. dollar demand by importers helped drag the Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan stocks slipped for the fourth straight session with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors watching anxiously from the sidelines as the index\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dropped below the 365-day moving average of 8,435 points.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The local unit is expected to move in a tight range,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par balancing between \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and recent appetite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Sing dollar was narrowly traded although strong May\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par industrial output data released earlier this week was a welcome\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sign for the Singapore economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The 1.74 to the dollar level was seen as a strong support\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par probably step in ahead of the level.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0902 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     105.64\tab  105.67\tab    +0.03\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7340\tab  1.7328\tab    -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr    30.810\tab  30.790\tab    -0.06\par  Korean won   1116.00\tab 1118.10\tab    +0.19\par  Baht\tab      39.09\tab   39.14\tab    +0.13\par  Peso\tab      43.12\tab   43.01\tab    -0.26\par  Rupiah\tab  8688.00\tab 8675.00\tab    -0.15\par  Ringgit\ta