\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Narrowly mixed again...on Fedwatch. \b0\par\par\uc2 948 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2000\par 03:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 27 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  were narrowly mixed in early business with local factors having \par \par \uc2  some influence, although volume was low ahead of the Fed. \par \par \uc2      The two-day Federal Open Market Committee begins its \par \par \uc2  two-day meeting later on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      A Reuters poll of all 29 primary dealers of U.S. Treasuries \par \par \uc2  showed none expected short-term rates to be changed this time, \par \par \uc2  but most saw a rise in August. \par \par \uc2      The Fed funds target rate is currently 6.5 percent and a \par \par \uc2  decision from this meeting is expected around 1815 GMT on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      The yen slipped overnight on rumours rating agencies were \par \par \uc2  ready to downgrade Japan's sovereign debt. \par \par \uc2      But the major rating houses said no action had been taken \par \par \uc2  after Japan's elections returned the ruling coalition to power, \par \par \uc2  albeit with a sharply reduced majority. \par \par \uc2      But yen bulls still happy and are looking for a strong \par \par \uc2  tankan next week to set the scene for an end to the zero \par \par \uc2  interest rate policy soon. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar was slightly weaker despite strong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par industrial output data on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Manufacturing output was up 20 percent in May on the year,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par boosting hopes the government's growth forecast of 5.5 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 7.5 percent this year will be met.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The data was not expected to have a major impact on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing dollar as the market had already had a preview through\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong exports in May, dealers said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They saw a tight range of 1.7300-1.7375 on fears of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of the 1.74 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar opened slightly lower after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced on Monday to raise key interest rates by 0.125\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percentage points, meeting market expectations, to curb\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation and stabilise financial conditions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Effective Tuesday, the discount rate will rise to 4.75\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent from 4.625 percent previously while the accomodation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with collateral rate will climb to 5.125 percent from 5.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In addition to fighting inflation, dealers said the cut was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also aimed at playing catch-up with the United States, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has raised rates by 1.75 percentage points since June 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said they broadly expected a T$30.760 to T$30.830\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Tracking regionals, the peso adopted a cautious stance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy-making meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Under the new tiering scheme, a 10 percent rate was set for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the first five billion pesos placed overnight, 8.5 percent for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the second five billion and seven percent for funds in excess\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 10 billion pesos.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It had previously borrowed at a straight 10 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said banks would have to bring down their peso\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deposit rates in line with the new tiering scheme, which in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par turn might drive depositors to shift to dollar assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso was expected to touch an initial support at 42.95\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to the dollar in coming days, and later aim to break the 43\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par psychological support.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won was slightly firmer as hefty dollar offers by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporters outpaced demand from importers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said exporters sold dollars for won to meet\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month-end financial demand locally. Moreover, the unit was also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par underpinned by the prospects for a trade surplus in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Local dealers said the country's trade surplus will likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be at least $1.0 billion in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was wedged in a tight range with little\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par direction as the market was dominated by range trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     European and Australian banks were head selling dollars to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par take profits while American names bid on dips.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the rupiah was unlikely to convincingly break\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par above 8,500 as concerns over its political and economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par upheavals kept long-term buyers on the sidelines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It's a very thin market to start with. Players are likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to take profits on the dollar at around 8,700 and buy it back\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par once it approaches 8,600," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The market is watching the Fed as there are few fresh\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par leads from the domestic front to trade on," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht was a touch firmer. Standard and Poor's MMS said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some players who accumulated the dollar in early May when it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was below 38.00 were selling to square positions ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par half-year book closings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the baht should also be underpinned by light\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capital inflows into Thailand's fixed income market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said the baht should be trapped in a tight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 39.00-39.130 range this week.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0801 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     105.67\tab  105.02