\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Early; Downside Bias Expected \b0\par\par\uc2 495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2000\par 03:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are narrowly mixed early Tuesday, and are likely to trade at the lower ends of their trading bands ahead of the Federal Reserve's policy meeting, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  While the Federal Open Market Committee is widely anticipated to keep interest rates steady at its two-day meeting, which starts later Tuesday, the market's focus has shifted to the FOMC's next meeting in August. The Fed is expected to resume its tightening cycle then, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The Fed, which has raised rates by a total of 175 basis points over the past year, is expected to announce Wednesday that there are still inflationary risks for the U.S. economy, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Traders will likely take a defensive stance and (are) prone to take profits on gains on the regionals, thus we see a slight weakening bias of the regionals versus the U.S. dollar," said Syetarn Hansakul, an economist at West LB Research. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, the rupiah is being buoyed by news of a civil state of emergency declared in the eastern Maluku islands to halt fierce fighting between Muslims and Christians that has left scores dead in recent days. \par \par \uc2  Around 0130 GMT (9:30 p.m. EDT Monday), the dollar was at 8,680 rupiah, unchanged from late Monday's level. The dollar is expected to find support around IDR8,660 on dollar-buying by local corporates and face resistance around IDR8,725, "unless we see more social tension," said a chief dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has declined to S$1.7332 from S$1.7344 late Monday. The U.S. dollar is expected to remain in its recent range of S$1.7310 to S$1.7360, as lingering fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  around S$1.7350 contribute to cautious trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht is steady at 39.130 baht versus the U.S. dollar. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely be hemmed in around THB39.050 to THB39.250 in the absence of market-moving incentives, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In South Korea, the dollar was at 1,118.50 won, marginally higher than KRW1,118.10 at Monday's close, and is expected to trade at KRW1,117 to KRW1,119. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has edged up to 42.945 pesos from Monday's close of PHP42.910, on an effectively lower Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight borrowing rate, dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  replaced Monday its single-rate borrowing system with a three-tier system. \par \par \uc2  Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at NT$30.785, down slightly from NT$30.797, as the market shrugged off an expected 12.5-basis-point increase each in two key interest rates by Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6r033tb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
