\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Shuffle along, Fed in focus. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,065 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2000\par 03:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 26 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  continued their recent narrowly mixed performance on Monday \par \par \uc2  with Japan's election containing no real surprises and keeping \par \par \uc2  dollar/yen within a narrow range. \par \par \uc2      The ruling coalition managed to hang onto its majority in \par \par \uc2  the Lower House although voters made their feelings clear by \par \par \uc2  handing Prime Minister Yoshiro Mori's ruling bloc a sharply \par \par \uc2  reduced majority. \par \par \uc2      It won 56.5 percent of seats against the two-thirds it held \par \par \uc2  before the election. \par \par \uc2      With the election out of the way the next big focus is the \par \par \uc2  Federal Open Market Committee meeting on Tuesday and Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      While Fed officials do not yet seem convinced the U.S. \par \par \uc2  economy is slowing the majority in the market do not expect the \par \par \uc2  Fed to move this time. \par \par \uc2      The Fed funds target rate is currently 6.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  However, there are a few who believe Greenspan might want to \par \par \uc2  send a strong message to the fresh stock market bulls and as no \par \par \uc2  change is so widely expected this would be a golden \par \par \uc2  opportunity. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was wedged in a narrow range, with demand for \par \par \uc2  dollars in non-deliverable forwards (NDF) trading kept its \par \par \uc2  upside capped in early trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the unit to move in a 1117-1125 range this \par \par \uc2  week and it is currently below its 14-day moving average of \par \par \uc2  1116.3. \par \par \uc2      The market is likely to watch closely banks' debt data \par \par \uc2  which the government said it would disclose by the end of June. \par \par \uc2      South Korea's finance ministry recommended that commercial \par \par \uc2  banks should put aside more than three trillion won ($2.86 \par \par \uc2  billion) in additional provisions against non-performing loans \par \par \uc2  (NPLs). \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah nudged up on a technical rebound as players took \par \par \uc2  profits from recent dollar gains. \par \par \uc2      But the reprieve would be short-lived as corporate demand \par \par \uc2  for dollars remained robust, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      Indonesia's slowly improving macro economic picture was \par \par \uc2  clouded by political problems which held the government back \par \par \uc2  from taking necessary steps to repair the badly-damaged \par \par \uc2  economy, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund said on Friday Indonesia's \par \par \uc2  economy was "pretty good" but stressed that the government \par \par \uc2  should speed up its recovery programme and sell off more assets \par \par \uc2  if it wanted to lure more foreign investments. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso tracked the regionals higher while the market \par \par \uc2  digested news about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new tiering scheme on \par \par \uc2  overnight borrowing rate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday that the first five billion \par \par \uc2  pesos worth of funds placed overnight with the agency would \par \par \uc2  receive a 10 percent rate and the second five billion pesos \par \par \uc2  would receive 8.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Funds in excess of 10 billion pesos would receive seven \par \par \uc2  percent while overnight lending rate would stay unchanged at \par \par \uc2  12.25 percent, it said. \par \par \uc2      The move effectively cut the borrowing rate from the \par \par \uc2  previous 10 percent, it said. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the news was likely to have limited impact on \par \par \uc2  the peso which looked set to test 42.93 in the near-term. \par \par \uc2      "Most players still look to buy dollars on dips. I don't \par \par \uc2  think the peso will be able to break 42.70 in the near-term \par \par \uc2  because that's the level where the market expects dollar \par \par \uc2  bargain hunters to emerge," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was flat in thin early trade and most companies \par \par \uc2  had closed their books for the first half of the year. \par \par \uc2  The market seemed to be digesting news that the main \par \par \uc2  opposition New Aspiration Party (NAP) would resign en masse on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday to force an early election, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      Some dealers said the news was unlikely to fluster the \par \par \uc2  market because an election must be called by November anyway. \par \par \uc2      Moreover, a spokesman for the Prime Minister Chuan Leekpai \par \par \uc2  said the government would still be able to push through next \par \par \uc2  year's budget by September. \par \par \uc2      Dealers expected the baht to move in a narrow range pending \par \par \uc2  the Federal Reserve's decision on interest rates on Wednesday \par \par \uc2  and the release of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly economic data on \par \par \uc2  Friday. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar retained its weak tone due to demand for \par \par \uc2  the U.S. dollar from local companies seeking to investment \par \par \uc2  abroad, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But players were reluctant to sell the unit aggressively on \par \par \uc2  fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the Sing dollar should remain trapped in \par \par \uc2  a range of 1.7300-1.7375 as the authority would probably step \par \par \uc2  in ahead of the 1.74 level. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was easier as recent consolidation in \par \par \uc2  local stocks dampened demand for the unit. \par \par \uc2  But the downside should be limited due to the stronger yen. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar is typically affected by movements in the yen \par \par \uc2  because Taiwan and Japan compete in the similar export markets. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  hike rediscount rate by 25 basis points in its policy board \par \par \uc2  meeting on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Justification is based on the recent rise of inflation to \par \par \uc2  1.6 percent in May and to catch up with U.S. interest rates," \par \par \uc2  SEB Merchant Banking said in a report. \par \par \uc2  "However, with leading index dipping for three straight \par \par \uc2  months and inflation largely an imported phenomenon, we rather \par \par \uc2  think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep rates on hold until the second \par \par \uc2  half," it said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0305 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     105.45\tab  104.41\tab    -0.99\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7318\tab  1.7312\tab    -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    30.775\tab  30.767\tab    -0.03\par  Korean won   1118.40\tab 1119.00\tab    +0.05\par  Baht\tab      39.05\tab   39.07\tab    +0.05\par  