\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Slightly; Set To Be In Tight Range \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2000\par 04:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar has weakened slightly against its U.S. counterpart early Monday in desultory trading, and is expected to remain within a tight trading band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market has turned skittish following the U.S. dollar's failure to remain buoyed late last week, after piercing through the key resistance levels of around S$1.7350 and S$1.7370, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0240 GMT (10:40 p.m. EDT Sunday), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7329, down from S$1.7311 late Friday in Asia, but within its recent trading range. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to cling to the S$1.7310 to S$1.7340 band for the rest of the day, following unverified rumors the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the S$1.7340 level Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Trading is expected to remain subdued as market participants are hesitant to open up new positions as the half-year end approaches, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Caution is also prevailing ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve's two-day policy meeting beginning Tuesday, dealers said. While the Fed is widely anticipated to leave interest rates unchanged, some market participants have already priced in the possibility of a 25-basis-point hike, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen's stability, after the Liberal Democratic Party-led coalition retained power in elections for Parliament's lower house Sunday, has provided little incentive for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to snap out of their recent trading ranges, dealers noted. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  Around 0240 GMT (10:40 p.m. EDT Sunday), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7329, up from S$1.7311 late Friday in Asia, but within its recent trading range. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (In an item timed at 0251 GMT, the direction of the U.S. dollar\par against the Singapore dollar was misstated.)\par -0- 26/06/00 05-59G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6q03453\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
