\par\par \b \uc2  Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Down Early; Rupiah Breaks Key Support \b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2000\par 03:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are lower early Thursday, with the Indonesian rupiah accelerating late Wednesday's slide after Bank Indonesia Governor Sjahril Sabirin was detained, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar muscled its way through the 8,700 rupiah level - which had proved a tough level to crack in recent weeks - to IDR8,728 at 0115 GMT (9:15 p.m. EDT Wednesday). The last time the dollar was around this level was in mid-May. \par \par \uc2  The latest twist in the politically-charged feud between President Abdurrahman Wahid's government and Bank Indonesia's Sjahril has scared investors. \par \par \uc2  Shahril has been detained for his alleged involvement in the Bank Bali scandal. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Sjahril's detention comes as a surprise given newly enacted laws that stress the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence and could hamper the progress of the country's financial reforms. \par \par \uc2  "The market's losing confidence," a dealer at a U.S. bank said. "There's no policy consistency." \par \par \uc2  The dollar could test IDR8,750 later in the day, although this could be stymied by Bank Indonesia's moves to defend the rupiah and the relatively modest interest to buy dollars at higher levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weaker rupiah has weighed on the Singapore dollar, the Thai baht and the Philippine peso, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A confluence of factors has also pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to break a key resistance level against the Singapore dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Having broken above S$1.7350 resistance, the U.S. dollar is likely to test S$1.7380-S$1.7390 later Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0135 GMT, the dollar was quoted at S$1.7350, up from S$1.7347 late Wednesday. Earlier, the dollar risen to a high of S$1.7362, but retreated on profit-taking and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Strong U.S. dollar demand linked to DBS Bank's recapitalization of unit DBS Thai Danu Bank, Singapore Power's A$2.1 billion acquisition of Australian power transmission company GPU PowerNet, and a reclamation project on Jurong Island have weighed on the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, the MAS' plan to introduce new legislation that forces Singapore's banks to separate their non-financial activities from their core bank and finance business has had little impact on the Singapore dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the dollar has broken resistance at 39.200 baht, but isn't expected to test the next resistance level at THB39.300 as offshore selling in U.S. dollars will likely cap the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around current levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at THB39.240, up from THB39.175 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In Manila, the dollar was quoted at 42.970 pesos, up from Wednesday's close at PHP42.830. \par \par \uc2  Unscathed by the regional market's weakness, the South Korean won has been buoyed by the 2% rally on the local bourse. The dollar was quoted at 1,118.80 won, down from Wednesday's close at KRW1,119.10. \par \par \uc2  Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at NT$30.813, little changed from Wednesday's close at NT$30.817. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6m031ob\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
