\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Rupiah bounces, others rangebound. \b0\par\par\uc2 819 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2000\par 11:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, June 1 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stole the show in late trade on Thursday as talk the government\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  might be exploring some form of capital control prompted \par \par \uc2  players to cover their short positions. \par \par \uc2      Other Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  shuffled along, driven by \par \par \uc2  commercial demand and moving within their recent ranges. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen\tab   retreated to six-week lows against the euro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  and its lowest level since May 19 against the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on worries about the health of Japan's financial sector.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Such fears were triggered after mid-sized Japanese insurer\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Daihyaku Mutual Life announced its closure, which spurred fears\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of more such bad news.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah gained almost three percent as players, spooked\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by the capital controls talk, rushed to cover short positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in thin offshore markets. Jakarta was closed for a holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore dealers said foreign banks in Asia and London\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par actively covered short rupiah positions against the U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the Singapore dollar after Horst Koehler, the new IMF\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par chief, said controls on capital movements were not "taboo", but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ought to be imposed only under special circumstances.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Koehler, who was on a visit to Bangkok, did not refer\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par specifically to the rupiah, but his remark further stirred a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market already primed by newspaper articles that Jakarta was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exploring the idea of controls to protect the rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the IMF's apparent softening in stance might\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remove a key obstacle if the government was planning any\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par controls, but they questioned how successful they would be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par given the country's openness and history of capital flight.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won closed lower against the dollar, influenced by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-deliverable forward (NDF) trade and renewed concerns about\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Hyundai Group , dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen's weakness also weighed on the won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Market jitters won't go away easily because of a family\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par feud at the Hyundai Group," said a local bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The commerce ministry announced a five-fold month-on-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise in the May trade surplus, putting the resurgent economy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back on course for a full year target surplus of $12 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The customs-cleared trade surplus jumped to a provisional\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $1.37 billion in May from a revised $247 million in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was firmer in late trade although volumes were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par light and range-trading was expected for Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The volumes are so low that a few million dollars of trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par changes the market direction," a Manila dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the country's political problems, including\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the ongoing hostage crisis and unrest involving Moslem\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par separatists in the south, would keep the market jittery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht edged up against the dollar, with trade confined\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to a narrow range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Technical analysts said the baht could head lower as a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par symmetrical triangle has formed on the charts, suggesting scope\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for a breakout to the 39.40/45 regions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Comments by the visiting IMF chief had limited impact.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He said earlier the Thai economy was on "a recovery path"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after its deep two-year recession but he was still concerned by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the level of bank debt and bad loans.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab   The Taiwan dollar was slightly easier\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as losses in Taipei stocks dampened sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The benchmark TAIEX\tab    ended off one percent,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reversing a three-day winning streak after the Nasdaq stumbled.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said the Taiwan dollar would be confined to a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tight range as interbank players turned cautious following\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar gained ground as U.S. investment funds and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks unwound long dollar positions, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the unit moved in a tight range amid a dearth of fresh\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par incentives with players expecting a range of 1.7280-1.7350 in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the near term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said corporate buying interest and continuous\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profit-taking activities in the greenback would keep the Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar supported.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0951 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     108.85\tab  107.26\tab    -1.46\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7313\tab  1.7337\tab    +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr    30.831\tab  30.813\tab    -0.06\par  Korean won   1132.10\tab 1129.40\tab    -0.24\par  Baht\tab      39.13\tab   39.17\tab    +0.10\par  Peso\tab      42.57\tab   42.61\tab    +0.09\par  Rupiah\tab  8450.00\tab 8640.00\tab    +2.25\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     108.85\tab  102.21\tab    -6.10\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7313\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.89\par  Taiwan dlr    30.831\tab  31.380\tab    +1.78\par  Korean won   1132.10\tab 1135.00\tab    +0.26\par  Baht\tab      39.13\tab   37.45\tab    -4.29\par  Peso\tab      42.57\tab   40.20\tab    -5.57\par  Rupiah\tab  8450.00\tab 6975.00\tab  