\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Ends Up Late; Gives Up Most Intraday Gains \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2000\par 11:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar gave up most of its intraday gains but managed to end slightly higher against its U.S. counterpart in quiet trading Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0850 GMT (4:50 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7335, down from S$1.7345 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Early in the day, the Singapore dollar gained along with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the back of rallies in Asian stock markets, which were sparked by Tuesday's 7.94% jump on the Nasdaq Composite Index. \par \par \uc2  Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also buoyed as exporters sold U.S. dollars in time for month-end bookkeeping, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar briefly dropped below the level of S$1.7300 before starting to climb again on the back of gains against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Local banks started selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the level of S$1.7345, pushing it back down again, dealers said. The selling sparked rumors of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally acts through local banks, dealers said there was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is likely to remain vulnerable to movements in Indonesia and elsewhere because of the island-state's increasingly close economic links to its neighbors. \par \par \uc2  "There is no reason for me to tell anybody to put his money into Sing dollars," said a trading desk chief at a European bank. "Sentiment is very weak." \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5v02o69\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
