\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Treading water, rupiah comes to. \b0\par\par\uc2 946 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2000\par 11:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 30 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  little changed in late trade on Tuesday, though the Indonesian \par \par \uc2  rupiah managed to pull off its lows after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  governor denied rumours of his resignation. \par \par \uc2      Assurances by Indonesian economic ministers that the IMF \par \par \uc2  was likely to release a delayed $400 million loan in June as \par \par \uc2  Jakarta had met all its economic reform targets also lent some \par \par \uc2  support to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Activity in G7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was dominated by the euro\tab  ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which rose to five-week highs against the dollar on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would raise interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates at its next meeting and on supportive comments from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European officials.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen\tab   regained lost ground against the dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bolstered by bullish economic data and an upbeat OECD report.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (OECD) projected that Japan will grow 1.7 percent in this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par calendar year, up from its previous forecast of 1.4 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It said in its semi-annual report that Japan's economy was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on a cyclical recovery path with deflationary pressures easing,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but warned that the country should continue to aim at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sustaining the recovery given uncertainties over economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prospects.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah fell near a May 12 low of 8,770 on reports the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Indonesia governor Sjahril Sabirin planned to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resign as early as Tuesday in connection with the high profile\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank Bali scandal.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But it managed to claw back some losses after the bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par denied the reports. A recovery in the stock market also helped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par improve sentiment, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Onshore dollar demand took the lead as most offshore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers remained sidelined due to the U.S. Memorial Day holiday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Chief economic minister Kwik Kian Gie said the recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decline in the rupiah was driven by psychological factors and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was not in line with economic fundamentals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He also expressed confidence that the IMF would proceed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the disbursement of a delayed $400 million loan tranche.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso ended lower as most players kept a cautious stance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due to lingering concerns over the domestic political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par situation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the market was unmoved by first quarter GDP\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data that showed the economy growing 3.4 percent year-on-year,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par broadly in line with expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso hit an intraday low of 42.90 before recovering\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par near the close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It was pretty quiet," one dealer said. "It was only range\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading...the low volume also suggests that most of the players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are very cautious."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the market was still quite edgy and worried\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over the domestic political situation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     One trader said any bad news could pull the peso past the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 43 level, but if the situation remained stable it could firm to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 42.60 or 42.70.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab    -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won rose slightly as dollar sales stemming from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stock market's rebound outweighed late buying by importers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dollar buying in the non-deliverable forward market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overseas prompted late short-covering, limiting the won's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par upside, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "In early trade, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market traced the movement of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the stock market," said a foreign bank dealer. "But sentiment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par changed when companies came in to settle their import deals."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers forecast the dollar/won range at 1,130-1,138 for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht was off its day low as high forward swap premiums\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore, which indicated that baht liquidity was tight,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par triggered some dollar offers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Any reprieve was unlikely to be sustained as most players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were still keen to buy the U.S. unit on dips, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen well-supported at 39.35 in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the near-term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market is focused on April economic data to be released\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by the Bank of Thailand on Wednesday and May price data from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Commerce Ministry on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The U.S. dollar remained perky against the Taiwan dollar on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par importer demand for month-end settlements.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Fears of foreign equity funds selling local stocks and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par uncertainty over Taiwan-China relations also dampened sentiment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the downside was limited on Tuesday due to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's last-minute \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said a dealer in Taipei.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR\tab   The Sing dollar was trapped in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tight range with dealers testing the downside at 1.7370 where\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they expected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action to kick in.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was sceptical of any major upside for the Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar as regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained under pressure.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the U.S. dollar would stay in favour ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. Federal Reserve meeting next month which was expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to yield another rate hike.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0935 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     106.59\tab  107.15\tab    +0.53\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7337\tab  1.7327\tab    -0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    30.884\tab  30.846\tab    -0.12\par  Korean won   1136.00\tab 1137.20\tab    +0.11\par  Baht\tab      39.25\tab   39.19\tab    -0.15\par  Peso\tab      42.77\tab   42.70\tab    -0.16\par  Rupiah\tab  8655.00\tab 8590.00\tab    -0.75\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     106.59\tab  102.21\tab    -4.11\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7337\tab  1.6640\tab    -4.02\par  Taiwan dlr    30.884\tab  31.380\tab    +1.61\par  Korean won   1136.00\tab 1135.00\tab    -0.09\par  Baht\tab      39.25\tab   37.45\tab    -4.59\par  Peso\tab      42.77\tab   40.20\tab    -6.01\par  Rupiah\tab  8655.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -19.41\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.01\par \f2