\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Dollar dominates, peso slides. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,004 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2000\par 04:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 24 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  were weaker on Wednesday, as glum local leads kept players \par \par \uc2  clinging on to the dollar. \par \par \uc2      Weaker regional stock markets were likely to depress \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the rest of the day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar edged up against the yen\tab   in early trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as the Nikkei fell below 16,000 for the first time\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since last May.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said there was no change in the ministry's stance that it would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par take appropriate action in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par needed.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rumours emerged on Tuesday that the ministry was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par considering raising the levels at which it was prepared to\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A stronger yen was seen adding pressure to the Nikkei,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which has lost 20 percent in the last six weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab   was a shade easier as players took a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wait-and-see stance ahead of an ECB meeting on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab    -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won was weaker against the dollar as players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rushed to sell the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the stock market dived,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Concerns over the unstable financial markets are rampant,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said a foreign bank dealer. "Dollar demand is dominating the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market in early trade as stocks fell sharply."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Korean shares got off to a bad start with the benchmark\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOSPI shedding more than four percent and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over-the-counter Kosdaq falling more than five percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at one point after a sharp overnight drop on the Nasdaq\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But some analysts said the won's downside looked limited.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think dollar/won shouldn't go much above here. I think\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it's going to trade in a range of 1,115 and 1,135 fairly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comfortably," said Patrick Bennett, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Warburg.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah dipped against the dollar after failing to break\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 8,400 in early trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the dollar/rupiah looked well-supported at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 8,345 where dollar bargain hunting was expected to emerge. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par upside was seen limited to 8,600 in the near term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the outlook remained shaky.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The rupiah seems to be trapped in a congestive area for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par now. But it can break out any time, given its vulnerability to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par both external and internal factors," said a dealer at a U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank Indonesia on Tuesday warned that the rupiah would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remain volatile until August as concerns over political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stability, and the economy continued to weigh on sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso weakened further despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's verbal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support as the market remained doubtful about the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political stability.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Phlippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earlier on Wednesday the peso would stay at current levels for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par now and could stabilise to 41 to the dollar when things\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par normalise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It will stay within this general area," he told a local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par radio station when asked about the direction of the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "If there is speculation, we'll come in to help the peso,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The unit breached key psychological support at 42 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar on Tuesday as dealers fretted over renewed Islamic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par militancy in the southern Mindanao region and the bombing of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shopping mall in Manila on Sunday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht nudged lower as the dollar remained very much in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par favour among investors who liquidated local stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the downside was limited by tight baht liquidity in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore market which prompted some players to unwind the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the macro economic front, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par set a medium-term core inflation target range of zero to 3.5\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent, which it said would help the country's exports and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par keep the Thai baht stable.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The target had limited impact on the baht as it was mostly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in line with market expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar edged lower to breach the 1.7350\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level, moving in lockstep with other regionals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But analysts expected limited downside as the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remained cautious about an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I think dollar/Sing should come back below 1.70. I think\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.71, 1.72 should be about the right level for dollar/Sing,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at a major bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar remained hostage to the fortunes of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stock market, which headed further south on Wednesday as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par semiconductor shares fell in line with a retreat in their U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par counterparts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Stock sales by foreign equity funds in light of the Nasdaq\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sell-off were likely to weigh on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par signs of easing tensions with China, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Signs of further trouble in the local banking sector with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local newspapers reporting over T$20 billion in overdue loans\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at Bank of Overseas Chinese would also dampen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment. The bank's shares were trading down T$0.31 at T$4.14\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at 0204 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was believed to have\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the Taiwan dollar in late Tuesday trade.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0215 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     106.55\tab  106.53\tab    -0.02\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7344\tab  1.7322\tab    -0.13\par  Taiwan dlr    30.799\tab  30.749\tab    -0.16\par  Korean won   1139.50\tab 1134.00\tab    -0.48\par  Baht\tab      39.31\tab   39.25\tab    -0.15\par  Peso\tab      42.75\tab   42.20\tab    -1.29\par  Rupiah\tab  8476.00\tab 8430.00\tab    -0.54\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 