\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Dips To 13-Month Low, Regains Ground Late \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2000\par 10:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar weakened Wednesday amid wider turmoil in regional stock and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, briefly falling to its lowest level in more than 13 months before regaining some ground, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rose to an intraday high of S$1.7363, its highest point since April 5, 1999, before slipping back to S$1.7358 around 0820 GMT (4:40 a.m. EDT). Late Tuesday in Asia, the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7318. \par \par \uc2  Like other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Singapore dollar has been weakened by declining share prices and concerns that interest rates in the U.S. will continue to rise, making Asian assets relatively less attractive. \par \par \uc2  But the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being bolstered by the country's political stability and sound economic fundamentals, even as \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Philippine peso are punished. \par \par \uc2  "It's quite resilient," a dealer said of the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "It has stabilized. I'm not sure we will go further (down) from here." \par \par \uc2  Dealers added that the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though unlikely, is forcing buyers of U.S. dollars to move cautiously. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of people are buying (U.S.) dollars on the dips," a dealer said. "They are testing the S$1.7365-70 level" to see if the MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Local \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  banks did sell U.S. dollars near the day's peak, the dealer said, but added that it was unlikely that the banks were acting at the behest of the MAS. The de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  by placing orders through local banks. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said that the U.S. dollar isn't likely to move above Wednesday's peak. "A lot of people are happy to sell dollars around those regions," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In fact, some players appear to be betting on MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and have sold the U.S. dollar short. Stop loss orders on those short positions could propel the U.S. dollar higher if it breaches S$1.7370, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 65/ 421-4802; christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5o02k7m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
