\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Lower; Pressured By Peso, Inflation Data \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2000\par 05:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- A swooning Philippine peso pulled down the Singapore dollar in its wake early Wednesday along with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0245 GMT (10:45 p.m. EDT Tuesday), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7352, up from S$1.7318 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The peso fell to its lowest point since October 1998, pressured by various factors such as the recent bombings in Manila and the Muslim insurgency in the south. At 0200 GMT, the U.S. dollar pushed past the psychological 42.50 peso level. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's woes were compounded by plunge in local share prices and surprisingly low inflation data for April, which suggest that a tightening of monetary policy isn't in the offing. \par \par \uc2  Data released late Tuesday show that annual inflation in April came to 1.1%, down from 1.2% in March. As a result, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore has no incentive to favor a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Simon Flint, an economist at the Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  "In the foreseeable term it's hard to see them tightening monetary policy," Flint said. The MAS uses the exchange rate, rather than interest rates, as its primary monetary policy tool. \par \par \uc2  Stocks are down sharply early Wednesday. The Straits Times Index is off 2.96%, or 55.63 points, at 1850.15 points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said, however, that the Singapore dollar is showing greater resilience to the regional market turmoil than other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A dealer at a U.S. bank said there are few long U.S. dollar positions against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  As a result, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the MAS to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely, the dealer said. "They won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  anytime soon," he said. "The market isn't long enough on dollars." \par \par \uc2  Even so, participants are likely to tread carefully for fear of provoking \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealer said, adding that the U.S. dollar is unlikely to move above S$1.7370 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso has been hammered by a spate of bombings in Manila and the hostage crisis in southern Philippines. There are also concerns about cronyism in the government. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 65/ 421-4802; christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5o02jrq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
