\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Ends Lower As Regional  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Weaken \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2000\par 12:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was dragged down by other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to end lower Tuesday as stock markets fell across most of Asia. \par \par \uc2  Around 0955 GMT (5:55 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7318, up from S$1.7277 late Monday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Expectations that interest rates will continue to rise in the U.S., together with declines in Asian stock markets, have pushed down local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as foreign investors liquidate their holdings and buy U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, the Straits Times Index fell 1.25%, or 24.10 points, to end at 1905.78 points, in reaction to interest-rate worries and declining stock prices in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the Singapore dollar to continue weakening in coming days. Further declines could provoke \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the level of S$1.7350, one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "I think people will be cautiously buying on dips," the dealer said. "I think you will see regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening across the board." \par \par \uc2  If the U.S. dollar breaches S$1.7350 without drawing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stop-loss orders above that level could quickly propel it to between S$1.7400 and S$1.7500, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Local economic data isn't expected to help the Singapore dollar, which lately has been reacting largely to other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Indonesian rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Inflation data for April is due to be released at 1030 GMT on Tuesday. However, inflation is likely to remain under control, meaning that the MAS will have no incentive to tighten exchange-rate policy, Citibank said in a research report. \par \par \uc2  Citibank said it expects annual inflation in April to remain unchanged at 1.2%. "An inflation rate below 2% is healthy and should not trigger any sustained policy tightening," Citibank said. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 65/ 421-4802; christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5n02kro\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
