\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Down On Stock Market Falls;Peso Hits 19-Mo Low \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 1,052 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2000\par 11:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The drubbing on regional stock markets continued to push Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  However, while a recovery in the yen provided a mild respite for some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late trading, faltering investor confidence in the Philippines sent the peso reeling to a fresh 19-month low. \par \par \uc2  The peso will likely remain frail as long as the conflict in the southern island of Mindanao between government military forces and Muslim rebels remains unresolved and bombings in Manila continue to raise concerns over national security, market observers said. \par \par \uc2  "It's difficult to envisage any significant improvement in the short term," Bank of America strategist Simon Flint said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 42.370 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up 46 centavos from Monday's close of PHP41.915. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the session, the dollar climbed to a fresh 19-month high of PHP42.375, its highest level since hitting PHP42.560 Oct. 23, 1998. \par \par \uc2  Market players expect more gloom for the peso. \par \par \uc2  "I wouldn't be surprised if the dollar hits PHP43 to PHP44, or even PHP46 this year," a dealer at an Asian bank said. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in soon to prop up the peso, despite Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura's remarks Tuesday that the authority isn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spot market to help support the peso and will continue to allow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain "market-determined." \par \par \uc2  Buenaventura said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday to defend the ailing local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars on the spot market. \par \par \uc2  Analysts, however, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can only provide temporary reprieve for peso. \par \par \uc2  "We are afraid the country needs more drastic solutions to help mend the peso weakness," said Syetarn Hansakul, an analyst at WestLB Research. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has breached every resistance level pegged by traders in daily spot market trading since April 24, following the abduction of 21 Western and Asian hostages from a Malaysian diving resort by Philippine Muslim rebels. \par \par \uc2  Philippine Finance Secretary Jose Pardo said Tuesday he believes the weak peso is a "serious concern" because it could erode the economic gains due to strong imports earlier in the year. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Separately, Buenaventura said further raising the overnight borrowing\par rate, which stands at 10%, remains an "option" to preempt another U.S.\par Federal Reserve interest rate increase. However, market observers said\par any increase in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  key rate would likely be aimed at\par arresting the peso's decline.\par - - 23/05/00 09-46G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The drop in the peso helped erode the Thai baht, although the Japanese\par yen's strength late in the day stemmed the Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fall, they\par added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was at 39.275 baht, up from THB39.000 late Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There was a lot of outright selling interest in the baht - buying in\par dollars, selling in the baht and bidding for baht swaps," the dealer at\par the Asian bank said. "People are concerned because of the outflow of the\par baht, due to the falling stock market and the problems in the\par Philippines."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Investors are also awaiting news from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary\par policy board, which is holding its first meeting late Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Thailand has adopted a flexible inflation-targeting monetary\par policy framework, and the target range for inflation may be set at the\par meeting. The upward limit of the inflation target is expected to be\par around 4%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  felt the brunt of regional stock market\par weakness, dealers said. However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regained some lost\par ground as the yen strengthened in late trading, they added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts also said the fall in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely be\par mitigated by profit-taking in U.S. dollar positions. Players have been\par building up long U.S. dollar positions in anticipation of more interest\par rate hikes in the U.S., after the Federal Reserve raised rates by half a\par percentage point last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There are people willing to sell (dollars)," Bank of America's Flint\par said. "You're not going to see a persistent slide in regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but it's difficult to see a sustained recovery for the\par moment."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South Korean won ended at its lowest level against the U.S. dollar\par in nearly 13 weeks as share prices on the Seoul stock market continued\par their recent downward spiral.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar finished at 1,134.40 won, up from Monday's close of\par KRW1,130.60 and its highest finish since Feb. 25, when it closed at\par KRW1,136.60.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overwhelmed by concerns over the health of the financial sector and\par the stock market, the won barely reacted to news Tuesday of a 12.8%\par growth in South Korea's first-quarter gross domestic product, dealers\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the Indonesian rupiah, the dollar rose to 8,445 rupiah, from\par IDR8,318 late Monday. The rupiah fell in line with other regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and as local companies bought dollars to service debt,\par dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Due to the weakened rupiah, Indonesia's domestic inflation rate is\par expected to creep up in May but will likely be capped below 2%, State\par Statistics Bureau Chief Sugito Suwito said Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the rupiah weakens to 12,000 rupiah (against the dollar), then\par inflation would be 2%, but the rupiah is unlikely to fall this far,"\par Sugito said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The decline in the Taiwan stock market and political tensions with\par China lifted the U.S. dollar, which closed at NT$30.749, from Monday's\par close of NT$30.709.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It was the second straight session of decline for the local dollar\par since the island's new government was sworn in Saturday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tried to limit the fall of the local\par dollar to around the NT$30.75 level, but offshore demand for U.S.\par dollars ran high because of its strength against regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7319, up\par from S$1.7277 late Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said they expect the Singapore dollar to continue its descent\par in coming days, although one said further declines could provoke\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the level of\par S$1.7350.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Netty Ismail; 65 421 4807\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5n02kor\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
