\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Down Early On Stock Mkt,Domestic Woes \b0\par\par\uc2 753 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2000\par 04:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are weaker against the dollar early Tuesday, pressured by declining regional stock markets, dealers said, adding that the Philippine peso and South Korean won have been rendered particularly vulnerable by domestic political and financial woes. \par \par \uc2  While most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to be confined to narrow trading bands in the absence of a clear short-term trend, the peso has resumed its rapid descent, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to a fresh 19-month high of 42.05 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up from Monday's close at PHP41.915. \par \par \uc2  A bomb blast last Sunday in the country's largest shopping mall has reinforced fears of political instability and concerns over national security, threatening the country's mediocre economic growth prospects and President Joseph Estrada's administration. An unresolved conflict in the south between government military forces and Muslim separatists has also damped investors' confidence in the country. \par \par \uc2  A trader said the dollar is set to climb further to PHP42.20 later in the day, but the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step in at that level to prevent a further slide. \par \par \uc2  But Philippine Finance Secretary Pardo hinted earlier in the day that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not be very keen to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this stage. While Pardo said the weak peso is a "serious concern" because it will affect the country's level of imports for the rest of the year, he added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  only "if it becomes absolutely necessary." \par \par \uc2  The slide in regional bourses has cast a pall on most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following the volatility in the U.S. stock market overnight, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is taking a back seat, following what is happening on the equity market," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In New York Monday, the Nasdaq Composite Index plummeted as much as 6.4% to a year-low of 3172.65 before recovering a bulk of its losses to end just 0.8%, or 26 points, lower at 3364. The Dow Jones Industrial Average pared a 250-point loss to close 0.8%, or 84.30 points, lower at 10542.55. \par \par \uc2  Against the Korean won, the dollar has climbed to 1133.90 won, the highest intraday level since it hit KRW1135.50 on Feb. 29. The dollar had closed at a 12-week high of KRW1130.60 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Looming potential problems at South Korean financial institutions due to ongoing concerns about needed reforms at investment trust companies and debt restructuring have weighed on the won, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But signaling its intention to expedite reforms of investment trust companies, South Korea's Finance and Economy Ministry will complete the planned injection of KRW4.9 trillion in public funds into ailing Korea Investment Trust Co. and Daehan Investment Trust Co. by end June, instead of September, as previously planned, the local Yonhap News Agency reported Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has weakened in sympathy with its regional counterparts, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0245 GMT (10:45 p.m. EDT Monday), the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.7340, up from S$1.7277 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  However, the Singapore dollar's fall will likely be tempered by fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it declines too steeply, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There's talk the authorities will cap it," a dealer said. "But looking at the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the board, I doubt it...It's not a Singapore dollar problem." \par \par \uc2  Even if the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it will unlikely be aggressive, the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the U.S. dollar is quoted at 8495 rupiah, up from IDR8318. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has also strengthened against the Thai baht, and was quoted at 39.18 baht compared with THB39.00 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht is poised to weaken further, but will likely face psychological resistance at THB39.50-THB40, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may defend the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around that level will likely cap the U.S. dollar's strength, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In Taiwan, the U.S. dollar has risen to NT$30.736, from its Monday's close at NT$30.709, following a 1.6% slide in Taiwan stocks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is, however, expected to remain active in market to maintain the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stability, some dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail; 65 421 4807 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5n02jyh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
