\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Ends Up; Long US Dlr Positions Liquidated \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2000\par 11:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar ended slightly stronger on Tuesday as participants took profit on some long U.S. dollar positions ahead of a widely expected interest rate hike in the U.S., dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was quiet as participants adjusted existing positions but didn't open new ones in advance of the meeting later Tuesday of the Federal Open Market Committee, the policy-making arm of the U.S. Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  Participants were all the more hesitant to take positions because Thursday is a public holiday in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The FOMC is widely expected to raise its key interest rate by 50 basis points. The size of the hike is expected to be influenced by U.S. inflation data to be released before the FOMC meets. \par \par \uc2  Around 0950 GMT (5:50 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7280, down from S$1.7296 late Monday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  A 50 basis-point U.S. rate increase will be neutral for the Singapore dollar, traders said, adding that they expected the U.S. unit to continue trading in a range of between S$1.7250 and S$1.7350. \par \par \uc2  However, the outlook for the likely level of the Singapore dollar has been clouded by the expectation that they \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the upper end of that range. \par \par \uc2  Because of the implicit threat of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , "It's very difficult to actually realize what is the general market position," said a trading desk chief at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.375%, up from 0.125% late Monday. The three-month rate was offered at 3.0000%, down from 3.0625%. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; +65-421-4802; christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5g02gq1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
