\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Must Weigh Downside Of  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Alan Yonan Jr. \par \uc2 884 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2000\par 11:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- Of the Southeast Asian nations considering \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up their faltering \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Indonesia may well be at the head of the queue. \par \par \uc2  But such meddling in the market is never without its costs, and Indonesia probably would suffer the harshest side effects by doing so, analysts say. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the region have been trending downward for several weeks in the face of broad-based dollar strength associated with rising interest rates in the U.S. In the case of Indonesia, Thailand and the Philippines, the pressure has been exacerbated by a host of local factors weighing on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  For Indonesia, the road has been perhaps the roughest, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experiencing wild swings amid growing investor uncertainty about the Jakarta government's ability to push through reforms and keep the economic expansion on track. \par \par \uc2  President Abdurrahman Wahid and his top advisors haven't helped matters by issuing confusing statements about exactly what the government was prepared to do to keep the rupiah from falling further. \par \par \uc2  Wahid's latest jawboning Tuesday appeared to provide some stability for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the dollar fell to about 8,500 rupiah after trading as high as IDR8,720 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  "I have asked the finance minister to persuade state banks to help (boost the rupiah)," Wahid said at a news conference. \par \par \uc2  "I have also asked Bank Indonesia to take necessary action to stop the rupiah weakening," he added, in a clear effort to prod \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the supposedly independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But with limited foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be limited by the amount it could spend defending the rupiah, said Steve Brice, treasury economist for Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  With a huge debt level more than 100% of GDP, Indonesia can ill afford to squander its reserves in what would likely be an ill-fated attempt to stop a stampeding market, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  Such a move also would go against the advice of the International Monetary Fund, which has been providing the discipline keeping Indonesia on the path to reform, Brice added. \par \par \uc2  "The IMF has been keeping Indonesia pointed in the right direction. The only way we'll see the rupiah strengthen is through a massive change in international investor confidence that comes with continued reform," he said. \par \par \uc2  Other possible quick fixes available to Indonesia, such as capital controls or a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board, also would do more harm than good because they would take the pressure off the government to stick with the tough IMF-prescribed reforms, Brice said. \par \par \uc2  John Dodsworth, the IMF's Indonesia representative, made the institution's position clear in comments Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We don't think the government should spend the money on defending an\par exchange rate when it has so many other choices to spend the money on,"\par he said in Brussels.\par   - - 16/05/00 09-38G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In contrast to Indonesia, government officials in Thailand and the\par Philippines probably are not overly concerned about the recent\par depreciation of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They might even quietly invite a certain amount of slippage to help\par the competitiveness of their exports, as long as inflation remains under\par control, analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Merrill Lynch's forecast for the Thai baht rests mainly on the\par performance of domestic inflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "As long as inflation does not exceed 4%, we believe that the Bank of\par Thailand can tolerate some baht weakness," said Supavud Saicheua, head\par of Thailand economics for Merrill Lynch.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand, which last week became the first financial crisis victim to\par emerge from IMF oversight, was rumored to have supported the baht\par through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the dollar rose above the\par THB39.000 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's motivation needs to be carefully examined,\par Supavud said in a research paper.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We believe the BOT's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to\par push the baht back below 39 per dollar does not signal an attempt to\par defend the baht at that level," he said. It appeared to be more of an\par effort to prevent excessive volatility and deter speculators from\par attacking the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , according to Supavud.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of Thailand's main objective is to keep the Thai economic\par recovery from stalling, and to do so it needs to keep interest rates low\par and the baht competitive against other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippines similarly probably will tolerate a certain amount of\par peso depreciation to keep its economic expansion moving forward, Brice\par said. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been under pressure lately from expectations of\par higher U.S. interest rates and government fighting with separatist\par rebels in the southern Philippines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar closed Tuesday at 41.630 pesos, its highest level since\par late October 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economic fundamentals, including the Philippines' improving budget\par situation, should be encouraging investment there, Brice said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Unfortunately for the authorities, the market is not looking at\par that," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will probably remain on the sidelines as long as the\par depreciation of the peso occurs in an orderly fashion, Brice said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the dollar hits 42 pesos over the coming week I don't think they\par will be worried at all."\par   -By Alan Yonan Jr. 65 421-4859; alan.yonan@dowjones.com\par -0- 16/05/00 11-08G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5g02gom\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
