\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Down Early Ahead Of Expected US Rate Hike \b0\par\par\uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2000\par 04:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are lower against the dollar early Tuesday on the eve of what most analysts expect will be an aggressive interest rate hike in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Local factors, such as political turmoil Indonesia and concerns over debt restructuring in Thailand also weighed on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Federal Reserve's policy making committee is widely expected to raise short-term interest rates by a half percentage point later Tuesday in an effort to slow rapid U.S. economic growth to a more sustainable rate. \par \par \uc2  Such a move would represent a tightening of policy for the Fed, which has limited its rate hikes to a quarter point since it began its latest round of tightening last June. \par \par \uc2  The strengthening dollar has taken its biggest toll on Indonesia and Thailand, where corporations that have high levels of dollar-denominated debt want to get their hands on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  before interest rates rise. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened higher against the rupiah and continued to gain ground in early trading. At 0145 GMT (9:45 p.m. EDT Monday), the dollar was quoted at 8,715 rupiah, up from IDR8,541 late Monday. Dealers expect a trading range of IDR8,500-IDR8,800 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the baht, the dollar was quoted at THB39.315, up from 39.250 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Corporates are frantically trying to get their hands on dollars," a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar moved precipitously close to the 1.7350-per-dollar level that dealers said could trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local monetary authorities. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar touched S$1.7333 within the first hour of trading before falling back to S$1.7314, up from S$1.7296 late Monday. Short-covering spurred by expectations of higher U.S. rates pushed the U.S. dollar up overnight in London and New York trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. dollar appreciation above S$1.7350 probably will be limited by concerns of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. The MAS was said to have entered the market last week to sell U.S. dollars when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose above that level. \par \par \uc2  The peso was lower on U.S. interest rate jitters, hitting its lowest level in nearly seven months. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 41.615 pesos after closing at PHP41.560 Monday. Continued gains could push the dollar to PHP41.700, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise against the New Taiwan dollar likely drew \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is quoted at NT$30.803, up from NT$30.767 at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  Local stock market gains could also help offset pressure on the New Taiwan dollar, which is coming in part from offshore activity where the U.S. dollar is generally well bid against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Against the South Korean won, the dollar is quoted at KRW1,115.90 up from KRW1,114.70 a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers cited weakness in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the major factor weighing on the won. A trading range of KRW1,113-KRW1,117 is expected Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By