\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Tracks Indonesian Rupiah To End Lower \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2000\par 11:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar ended weaker Monday in a day of trading that saw its ups and downs shadow those of the more volatile Indonesian rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0850 GMT (4:50 p.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7296, up from S$1.7243 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Although the Singapore dollar mimicked the rupiah, its swings were far more moderate, and its losses were capped by expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  above the level of S$1.7300. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has been whiplashed by a series of statements by senior officials. On Monday, President Abdurrahman Wahid said he wouldn't impose capital controls to steady the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  These remarks followed a statement last week by economics czar Kwik Kian Gie, who said he couldn't honestly ask foreign investors to put their money into Indonesia. On Monday, Kwik was quoted as saying he was ready to resign if his policies didn't work. \par \par \uc2  Both the Singaporean and Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may get some respite in the next day or so as investors liquidate long U.S. dollar positions ahead of the meeting of the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been hammered by expectations that the FOMC would raise the Federal funds target rate by 50 basis points at its May 16 meeting, and that it likely will continue raising rates later in the year. \par \par \uc2  Singapore is scheduled to release a string of economic statistics that analysts say are all likely to be positive, starting with retail sales data on Monday and continuing with first quarter gross domestic product Friday and exports on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  But with the island-state seen as being influenced largely by regional developments, local economic data aren't expected to offer much support to the Singapore dollar, said Philip Wee, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  "Indonesia is the one that is creating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  uncertainty in the region," Wee said. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.375%, up from 1.250% late Friday. The three-month rate was offered at 3.000%, down from 3.0625%. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 65/ 421-4802; christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5f02edm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
