\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Cautious after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk. \b0\par\par\uc2 790 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2000\par 04:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , May 12 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  were mostly easier early on Friday on persistent dollar demand \par \par \uc2  from both offshore and onshore players. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had briefly staged a moderate rebound as \par \par \uc2  players became cautious following talk of central banks in \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Thailand and Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      The dollar retreated from Thursday's two-month high of \par \par \uc2  around 110.08 yen on profit taking. \par \par \uc2      U.S. retail sales fell for the first time in almost two \par \par \uc2  years in April, offering some hopes that the rapidly-expanding \par \par \uc2  economy may have begun to slow. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab   remained bearish against the dollar after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held interest rates steady and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par officials failed to offer fresh clues about a possible plan to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support the ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won opened lower amid heavy dollar buying in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-deliverable forward (NDF) market as dealers returned from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday's holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen's weakness on Thursday sparked NDF won selling in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overseas trade, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the dollar's upside in the Korean spot market was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limited by the unwiding of dollar positions, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The unit was trading in a lacklustre mood with players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forecasting a range of 1,109-1,111 throughout the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar was firmer after market rumours on Thursday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend it from 13-month lows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers saw range-trading for the Sing ahead of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend, trading between 1.7210-80 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Those who had positions would have squared them yesterday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par so we're not going to see much action today before the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend," a dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab   The rupiah slipped through the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 8,400 per dollar mark again, despite early dollar profit-taking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell to a seven-month low on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market remained bearish on high corporate demand for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars and dampened sentiment over the country's political and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic outlook.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A local newspaper reported that analysts had urged the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government to revert to a managed floating rate system to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prevent further sharp falls in the rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso retained its weak tone to hover around the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 18-month low hit on Thursday on continued rate jitters ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Fed's meeting next week and an armed conflict in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par southern Mindanao region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market will focus on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary board\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meeting with some analysts anticipating a 20 to 30 basis point\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hike.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bank raised its key overnight rates by 25 basis points\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earlier this month on expectations the Fed would raise rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aggressively.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the peso would remain under pressure and could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par touch its next critical support at 41.50 on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar nudged up following a sharp decline on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday, taking positive cues from a stronger yen and a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rebound in the stock market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan stocks rallied in early Friday trade, mirroring Wall\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Street's strong rebound overnight, but brokers cautioned over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par uncertain Taiwan-China ties and Wall Street's direction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Standard and Poor's MMS said in a report the weaker dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could prompt a breach of resistance at 30.70 on Friday with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par next resistance seen at 30.68.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's commitment to defending its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also seen supporting the Taiwan dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht kept its stance above the key 39.00 per dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par despite downward pressure from sustained dollar demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said near-term support for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remained at 39.00 per dollar, with resistance at 38.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was set to release data on foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reserves at 0800 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0203 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     108.13\tab  109.74\tab    +1.49\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7262\tab  1.7260\tab    -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    30.727\tab  30.752\tab    +0.08\par  Korean won   1111.30\tab 1112.50\tab    +0.11\par  Baht\tab      38.95\tab   38.90\tab    -0.13\par  Peso\tab      41.45\tab   41.35\tab    -0.23\par  Rupiah\tab  8410.00\tab 8390.00\tab    -0.24\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     108.13\tab  102.21\tab    -5.47\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7262\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.60\pa